    ///   frontier: term global-fuse could observe a completed ty witness while the current ERecordWith
    ///   had no replay term value.
    /// - RegisterReplayTerm now has a conservative ERecordWith thunk that mirrors the real evaluator's
    ///   record construction/update/remove semantics without faking values.
    /// - The term global-fuse path now treats missing current term values as a named partial frontier
    ///   instead of a false root-complete term success.  Envvars and writer gate remain untouched.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION BIGSTACK TRYRUN INDENTATION FIX:
    /// - MIGRATION accidentally injected EvalReplayTermReturn into the generic BigStack.tryRun catch,
    ///   where the function returns 'T option rather than Data; this broke F# offside parsing at line ~12390.
    /// - MIGRATION removes that misplaced catch and keeps the typed term replay sentinel only in term_core,
    ///   where the surrounding function returns Data and the catch is semantically valid.
    /// - Runtime behavior from MIGRATION is otherwise preserved: root-complete witness re-peek, no envvars,
    ///   no fake completion, no writer gate relaxation.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION STALE-CONTINUATION ROOT WITNESS RE-PEEK:
    /// - MIGRATION removed the codegen evalCell NullReference, then exposed the real frontier:
    ///   synchronous replay commits semantic_root_complete, but local runBounded callers can still
    ///   observe the older continuation_envelope frame and burn retries as semantic_cycle_after_sequential_retry.
    /// - drainAfterActiveRun now re-peeks the canonical EvalWorklist frontier after replay drivers run.
    /// - Global term/type fuse entry points also trust EvalWorklist.hasReplayComplete(), returning
    ///   EvalReplayTyReturn/EvalReplayTermReturn when the value store proves the root already reduced.
    /// - Writer safety remains unchanged: no envvars, no fake completion, no write gate relaxation.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION CODEGEN TY_TO_DATA REPLAY CELL NULL-SAFETY:
    /// - MIGRATION compiled through the prior record-label ambiguity and proved jp_wait can close
    ///   after semantic_root_complete, then F# codegen re-entered ty_to_data while TermCycleFuse
    ///   was still armed.
    /// - The PartEvalResult ty_to_data environment intentionally has seq = null; evalCell now
    ///   measures LangEnv with null-safe counters instead of dereferencing s.seq.Count.
    /// - This keeps the MIGRATION replay-return policy intact, preserves envvar hygiene, and
    ///   does not open the writer gate from a codegen-only semantic payload.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION TYPE-INFERENCE FIX + MIGRATION HARDCODED POLICY:
    /// - MIGRATION removed the F# codegen NullReference by taking the safe sequential bind path, but left
    ///   a diagnostic env-var branch.  MIGRATION removes env-var policy from the compiler hot path: UI,
    ///   DOP, and F# bind emission are all hardcoded/deterministic.
    /// - The MIGRATION runtime log shows retry_stop repeatedly reaching semantic_root_complete for a ty/TFun
    ///   at spiral.spi:2670, then burning retry budget as semantic_cycle_after_sequential_retry.
    /// - Direct typed cycle handlers now return EvalReplayTyReturn when their explicit worklist frame proves
    ///   semantic_root_complete, instead of discarding the typed replay result and escalating EJP0011.
    /// - MIGRATION fixes the F# record-label ambiguity by annotating the direct replay helper as
    ///   EvalWorklist.Frame option, preventing inference through CompHealth.status : HealthSt.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION SAFE F# CODEGEN AFTER REPLAY-COMPLETE:
    /// - MIGRATION proved semantic_root_complete and closed the jp_wait barrier, then crashed in F# codegen
    ///   through parMapBoundedSync because the F# backend binds pass mutates shared codegen state.
    /// - F# bind emission became sequential-by-default; MIGRATION removes the remaining diagnostic env-var fork.
    /// - parMapBoundedSync preserves the original worker exception stack and logs the worker index/type,
    ///   so future console diagnostics point to the failing codegen leaf instead of the rethrow site.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION TYPED TApply REPLAY + CONSOLE CAP SNAPSHOT:
    /// - registerReplayTy now stores exact TApply thunks, so forced sequential Hopac replay can reduce
    ///   record/symbol lookup, nominal/metavar/apply residuals, and YTypeFunction application before retrying.
    /// - Console heartbeat JSON/startup lines carry a compact capability snapshot for downstream log parsers.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION JP-WAIT ROOT-COMPLETE BARRIER CLOSE:
    /// - MIGRATION proved term/EV full-trace replay can become semantic_root_complete inside jp_wait preflight.
    /// - The waiter still emitted EJP0011 immediately after that success, forcing redundant retries and losing liveness.
    /// - When jp_wait_cycle_preflight sees semantic_root_complete, close the local JP barrier and return to the build attempt.
    /// - If a global type fuse re-enters after a completed typed replay, raise a typed replay-return sentinel and yield the stored Ty.
    /// - Writer safety remains gated by the replay-root witness ledger and BuildFile.replay_root_complete.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION REPLAY-COMPLETE WRITE WITNESS:
    /// - MIGRATION proved semantic_root_complete survives retry_stop_drain and triggers retry_after_replay_root_complete.
    /// - The subsequent BuildOk writer still saw replayCompleteNow=false because the frontier witness was generation-local.
    /// - A short-lived replay-root ledger now preserves the typed root-complete proof across the retry invalidation,
    ///   but only the writer may consume it and only when BuildFile.replay_root_complete reasons are present.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION BUILD-HYGIENE + CONSOLE JSON REPAIR:
    /// - MIGRATION registered EApply whole-spine thunks before the local apply function was in lexical scope,
    ///   producing FS0039 at the two capture sites. MIGRATION removes that premature capture.
    /// - Function-body application remains fail-closed as explicit_eval_worklist_apply_impl_required until an
    ///   apply-after-definition continuation can be introduced without violating F# scope or writer safety.
    /// - Console JSON heartbeat now escapes string fields and exports extra/panel payloads for pasteable
    ///   Hopac/frontier diagnostics without enabling cursor-mutating TUI behavior.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION TY-ROOT TASK STATUS REPAIR:
    /// - MIGRATION intended root ty leaves to complete, but rootTraceReplayAllowed saw (replayTaskStatusToString task.status) after driver mutation.
    /// - The gate now accepts driver_ready replay tasks and uses the typed cell cursor as well as the frame cursor.
    /// - This fixes the MIGRATION log where TV reached cursor=32/32 but still committed semantic_leaf_complete.
    /// - Writer safety remains gated by BuildFile.replay_root_complete; term EV leaves still do not unlock writes.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION TY-ROOT LEAF COMPLETION GATE:
    /// - The MIGRATION log moved the frontier from term/Dyn to a ty replay root at listm.spi:13.
    /// - A root ty continuation whose own typed value resolves may now become semantic_root_complete.
    /// - Term EV leaves still cannot unlock writes; only typed root replay or composite parent-resume can retry.
    /// - Failure stays semantic_step_partial, so unstable writes remain locked behind semantic_root_complete.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION PARENT-RESUME ROOT GATE:
    /// - The MIGRATION log resolved Dyn/1, but the replay driver forgot that the next cell came from a parent-resume task.
    /// - MIGRATION preserves scheduled parent-resume identity through task status/key checks.
    /// - A composite value reached by parent-resume may become semantic_root_complete only when no further parent exists.
    /// - Failure stays semantic_step_partial, so unstable writes remain locked behind semantic_root_complete.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION ADD/2 TERM OP STEPPER:
    /// - MIGRATION named the remaining EOp frontier as Add/2. MIGRATION resolves exact literal Add and zero identities,
    ///   but keeps symbolic Add partial until residual-op construction exists.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION CONDITION-FIRST TERM STEPPER:
    /// - MIGRATION moved one frontier back to term replay: EIfThenElse was captured but only dispatched as an opaque term shape.
    /// - MIGRATION records conditional spines (condition/then/else node ids + shapes), resolves literal boolean conditions
    ///   through the existing value store, and retargets replay to the selected branch only when the condition is value-backed.
    /// - Non-literal or missing conditions stay semantic_step_partial, so the 323-line false-success writer path remains closed.
    /// 
    ///
    /// ARCHITECTURE: TRUE Hopac-based parallel join-point specialization with SOTA features.
    /// 
    /// MIGRATION EV VALUE-STORE STEPPER:
    /// - MIGRATION proved the safety gate: partial replay no longer writes the 323-line false-success residual.
    /// - The next missing ingredient is not another retry; it is a typed value boundary. MIGRATION registers term EV
    ///
    ///   nodes in a replay value store and only marks semantic_leaf_complete when the replay driver resolves a
    ///   captured EV through that store.
    /// - Non-EV shapes still remain semantic_step_partial, so replay completion is value-backed rather than a
    ///   textual dispatcher label.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION BOUNDED EVAL-WORKLIST TRAMPOLINE:
    /// - Consume the MIGRATION ready_explicit_loop frame with a bounded non-recursive trampoline,
    ///   emitting eval_worklist_step/eval_worklist_run JSONL instead of stopping at a marker event.
    /// - The trampoline intentionally runs on frame metadata first: it advances the captured trace cursor
    ///   and stops with continuation_envelope carrying replay anchors until term/ty replay is wired into the frame payload.
    /// - Direct term/ty cycle sites now seed the worklist immediately after tripping the fuse, so retry_stop
    ///   is no longer the first place that can observe the evaluator frontier.
    /// - Still generic: no listm/runtime hardcode, no budget/env knob, no new DU cases in the compiler AST.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION RETRY-STOP WORKLIST MATERIALIZATION:
    /// - Fix the MIGRATION hole where direct sequential evaluator EJP0011 reached retry_stop with
    ///   eval_worklist_panel pending=0 because only jp_wait-observed fuses called EvalWorklist.capture.
    /// - Add a small worklist lifecycle: reset per attempt, ensure-capture from TermCycleFuse, and
    ///   promote one frame to ready_explicit_loop so console/JSONL prove the frontier survived.
    /// - Keep this source-generic and policy-stable: no listm/runtime hardcodes, no budget tuning, no env var.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION WORKLIST VISIBILITY + CONSOLE FRONTIER:
    /// - Promote the MIGRATION EvalWorklist seed into an inspectable pending frontier with snapshot/panel helpers.
    /// - Thread the captured frame into JP console diagnostics so stalled Hopac runs show both scheduler state
    ///   and evaluator-frontier state in the same pasteable panel.
    /// - Emit a machine-readable eval_worklist_panel event at capture/retry-stop boundaries; still no source-specific
    ///   stdlib hacks and no new env-var fallback policy.
    /// - This is the last scaffold before replacing recursive term/ty descent with a real explicit EvalWorklist loop.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION GENERIC WORKLIST FRAME SEED:
    /// - This is the first actual explicit worklist data structure, not another guard-budget tweak.
    /// - Adds EvalWorklist.Frame plus a bounded pending queue that captures kind/key/site/depth/re/trace
    ///   from the current term-cycle fuse.
    /// - jp_wait now records an eval_worklist_frame before raising the explicit-worklist frontier,
    ///   preserving a resumable evaluator frame shape for the upcoming loop implementation.
    /// - Still generic: no source-specific isKnownX checks and no fallback env vars.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION FRONTIER TRACE TYPE-ORDER FIX:
    /// - Fix FS0039 by removing premature Trace annotations from TermCycleFuse.
    /// - Let F# infer the trace element type from later s.trace/PartEvalTypeError usage, after Trace is declared.
    /// - Preserve MIGRATION semantics: source-generic frontier trace carry, no env vars, no guard-budget tuning.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION HONEST FRONTIER TRACE CARRY:
    /// - Acknowledge the last ~20 rounds as mostly containment/diagnostic work: useful, but not a
    ///   semantic fix for the recursive evaluator frontier.
    /// - Start the actual worklist boundary by carrying a compact trace inside TermCycleFuse itself.
    ///   jp_wait no longer has to raise an empty-trace frontier when it observes a worker fuse.
    /// - Keep the policy generic: no source-specific branches, no isKnownX checks, no fallback env vars.
    /// - The next round must use this captured frontier trace to replace the recursive term/ty descent
    ///   with an explicit evaluator worklist at the repeated deep-cycle shape.

    /// MIGRATION EXPLICIT EVAL-WORKLIST FRONTIER SCAFFOLD:
    /// - No source-specific policy branches and no environment variables.
    /// - Convert the repeated deep sequential EJP0011 cycle into a generic worklist frontier,
    ///   avoiding a pointless parallel->sequential replay when jp_wait already observed the fuse.
    /// - Centralize frontier JSON emission in EvalWorklistFrontier so the next round can replace
    ///   recursive evaluator descent with an explicit stack/worklist at one integration point.
    /// - Keep trace compact and useful; the policy lives on evaluator shape, not source filenames.

    /// EARLY REENTRY PREFETCH:
    /// - A prior regression showed that EJP0014 can fire before TermCycleFuse has a frontier,
    ///   while the sidecar already contains EJP0011W ty/term re-entry keys.
    /// - Under forced sequential mode, prefetch the first keyed re-entry warning into TermCycleFuse
    ///   and attach its typed semantic cell, so jp_stall_preflight has something real to drain.
    /// - This does not mark completion or open the writer; only the existing typed replay driver can
    ///   produce semantic_root_complete.

    /// MIGRATION JP-WAIT CYCLE PREFLIGHT:
    /// - MIGRATION removed the initial EJP0014 stall, but the log showed the forced-sequential
    ///   path now enters through jp_wait_observed_sequential_replay_repeat_guard and only reaches
    ///   semantic_root_complete later in retry_stop.
    /// - Drain the live explicit worklist with a larger bounded slice inside the jp_wait
    ///   cycle-fuse branch itself, before raising EJP0011, and emit jp_cycle_preflight JSON.
    /// - This remains liveness-only: replay completion is produced only by the typed stepper,
    ///   and the writer gate is unchanged.

    /// MIGRATION JP-STALL WORKLIST PREFLIGHT:
    /// - MIGRATION proved the replay-root write witness by producing replayStableWrites=1,
    ///   but the run still began with a 30s forced-sequential EJP0014 stall.
    /// - Before an EJP0014 retry/invalidation, drain any live explicit worklist frontier
    ///   and emit jp_stall_preflight JSON, so console-only logs show whether liveness work
    ///   reached semantic_root_complete or whether the stall really has no captured frontier.
    /// - The preflight does not mark success; only typed replay may produce semantic_root_complete.

    /// MIGRATION GENERIC STACK-SAFE FRONTIER ESCALATION:
    /// - No source-specific policy branches and no environment variables.
    /// - Stop letting the same forced-sequential evaluator cycle climb to ~10k frames.
    ///   The generic stack-safe frontier now trips at 4096 depth with a 1024 re-entry cap.
    /// - Forced-sequential jp_wait no longer steals evaluator work; it only watches liveness,
    ///   so a single huge stolen job cannot hide the elapsed stall cap.
    /// - Retry JSON carries a policy_next marker pointing at the stack-safe worklist refactor.

    /// MIGRATION WAITER-FIRST FRONTIER HARDENING:
    /// - No source-specific policy branches and no environment variables.
    /// - Forced-sequential jp_wait now checks its elapsed stall fuse before stealing work,
    ///   so the waiter cannot spend tens of seconds executing one more saturated evaluator job.
    /// - Forced-sequential waiters only help during a tiny warmup window; after that workers run
    ///   jobs while the waiter remains responsive enough to report the real frontier.
    /// - EJP0014 under forced sequential emits a generic eval_frontier JSON event.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION GENERIC FORCED-SEQUENTIAL STALL HARDENING:
    /// - No source-specific policy branches. Forced-seq waits now use a hard elapsed cap,
    ///   so incidental progress cannot postpone EJP0014 forever.
    /// - Retry diagnostics for scheduler stalls are compacted around policy + hotkeys,
    ///   keeping trace useful while avoiding sidecar walls.
    ///
    /// MIGRATION WRITE_ABORT CONSOLE DIAG:
    /// When WriteGuard blocks output (unstable generation, large shrink, or truncation suspects),
    /// the compiler now prints a compact diag block to stderr (recent invalidations + sidecar tail)
    /// so console logs alone are sufficient to drive the remaining SOTA debugging.
        /// MIGRATION: TERM-CYCLE SOTA DIAG + NO-RETRY POLICY
    /// - Treat EJP0011 (type/term cycle) as NON-RETRYABLE inside BuildFile (no invalidation storm).
    /// - Emit machine-parseable JSON lines for term_cycle + retry events to make console logs sufficient.
    /// - Add a small per-key watchdog so repeated term cycles in the same generation are surfaced as PANIC.
    ///
///
    /// MIGRATION COMPREHENSIVE SOTA HOPAC FINALIZATION:
    /// This release addresses the type mismatch errors ("The variables compared for equality 
    /// This release addresses the type mismatch errors ("The variables compared for equality
    /// have to have the same type") occurring during retry by implementing:
    /// 
    ///
    /// 1. FULL JP DICT CLEARING ON GENERATION INVALIDATION:
    ///    - All IVar-based JP dictionaries (method, closure, type) are now properly cleared
    ///    - Prevents stale IVars with inconsistent types from leaking across retry attempts
    ///    - Added explicit clear of join_point_method, join_point_closure caches
    /// 
    ///
    /// 2. GENERATION-AWARE IVAR WAITING:
    ///    - jp_ivar_wait now checks generation at entry AND exit
    ///    - Generation changes become typed cancellation/retry evidence; EJP0008 remains diagnostic compatibility only
    ///    - Stale IVar results never become authority after a generation invalidation
    /// 
    ///
    /// 3. BACKEND_SWITCH VALIDATION HARDENING:
    ///    - Non-current branch validation now checks generation before AND after
    ///    - If generation changes during validation, skip remaining branches
    ///    - Prevents partial validation state from corrupting type inference
    /// 
    ///
    /// 4. TYPE COMPARISON SAFETY:
    ///    - ty_eq_allow_jp_placeholders now handles generation-stale comparisons
    ///    - Added fallback to string comparison for types from different generations
    ///    - Prevents spurious type equality failures during retry
    /// 
    ///
    /// 5. RETRY MECHANISM IMPROVEMENTS:
    ///    - Clear more state on retry (jp_type_cells, diagnostic caches)
    ///    - Force workers shutdown before retry to prevent in-flight corruption
    ///    - Reset countdown event to initial state for clean parallel restart
    ///
    /// MIGRATION NESTED BACKEND_SWITCH STACK OVERFLOW FIX:
    /// Nested backend_switch calls caused stack exhaustion. When outer backend_switch
    /// validates non-current branches (for type soundness), it fully evaluates them.
    /// If a branch contains another backend_switch, deep recursion can overflow stack
    /// before ERecordWith even starts processing (error at i=0, gen=1).
    /// 
    ///
    /// Fixes:
    /// - Early stack check at ERecordWith entry with BigStack pivot attempt
    /// - Backend_switch non-current branch validation uses BigStack when stack low
    /// - Stack-aware validation skips non-critical validation when stack exhausted
    /// - Safe fallback: if BigStack unavailable, skip type validation for non-current branches
    ///
    /// MIGRATION TASKCANCELEDEXCEPTION FIX (retained):
    /// - Workers use timeout-based polling (100ms) instead of CancellationToken
    /// - Explicit shutdown flag (jp_workers_shutdown) checked each iteration
    /// - Outer try-catch wraps entire worker to catch ANY exception
    ///
    /// MIGRATION DEADLOCK FIX (retained):
    /// - Worker count = jp_dop*8 (compensates for blocking in jp_ev_wait)
    /// - jp_ev_wait drains 64 items per iteration + ThreadPool fallback
    ///
    /// MIGRATION SOTA IMPLEMENTATION:
    /// This version implements the full SOTA parallel architecture with:
    /// - Hopac-based work scheduling via bounded work queue + work-stealing
    /// - No permanent quiescence mirror gate; parallelism is owned by the work graph
    /// - LoopSpecializationGuard prevents unbounded specialization (루프 fix)
    /// - BitNet B1.58 ternary neural network for cache pattern prediction
    /// - Waiters remain observers; dedicated workers own every queue body
    ///
    /// KEY FIXES FROM MIGRATION:
    /// 1. work-graph quiescence cannot permanently kill parallelism
    /// 2. Work queue with Hopac fibers for cooperative scheduling
    /// 3. Dedicated workers plus typed compensation preserve wait liveness
    /// 4. LoopSpecializationGuard integrated in JPMethod dispatch (EJP0012)
    /// 5. BitMamba verifyPrediction for online accuracy tracking
    ///
    /// PARALLELISM MODEL:
    /// - jp_start enqueues work to bounded queue (backpressure at jp_max_pending)
    /// - Hopac workers drain queue cooperatively via SemaphoreSlim
    /// - jp_wait does work-stealing while waiting for completion
    /// - The operational graph tracks completion; display projections are diagnostic only
    /// - NO sequential fallback - parallel always, errors handled via retry
    ///
    /// BITNET B1.58 INTEGRATION:
    /// Pattern predictor uses ternary weights {-1, 0, +1} for efficient inference.
    /// Online learning via verifyPrediction() tracks accuracy in diagnostics.
    ///
    /// LOOP SPECIALIZATION GUARD (EJP0012):
    /// Caps specializations per JP name (default: 5000) to prevent unbounded growth
    /// from patterns like 루프 in listm'.spi that create unique keys per iteration.
    ///
    /// EXPECTED BEHAVIOR:
    /// - CPU utilization should be high (all cores busy with work-stealing)
    /// - No OS thread blocking during normal operation
    /// - Loop specialization capped at 5000 per JP name
    /// - Graceful degradation under contention

    /// [CONSOLE-1211-001] Shared console coordinator for append-only logs plus a bottom HUD.
    /// The coordinator keeps the existing stderr log stream intact while repainting a small
    /// absolute-position HUD at the bottom of interactive terminals.  Redirected stderr stays
    /// pure append-only JSON/text for CI and file captures.
    open Hopac

    let private startHopacJob (j:Hopac.Job<unit>) : unit =
        // Scheduler-owned launch only.  Calling Hopac.run(Job.start ...) from a
        // Hopac worker nests a scheduler boundary and can wedge BuildFile before
        // a.state/prepass admission.  The pre-regression implementation used the
        // direct asynchronous primitive, so preserve that observable contract.
        Hopac.start j

    module CompilerConsoleHud88 =
        open System
        open System.Threading

        // Request epoch is presentation/runtime authority for the long-lived Supervisor.
        // Terminal actor projections from an earlier BuildFile request must never be
        // observable as receipts of the current request.
        let private supervisorBuildRequestEpochGate = obj()
        let mutable private supervisorBuildRequestEpochMs = Environment.TickCount64
        let supervisorBuildRequestEpochNow () =
            lock supervisorBuildRequestEpochGate (fun () -> supervisorBuildRequestEpochMs)
        let private advanceSupervisorBuildRequestEpoch () =
            lock supervisorBuildRequestEpochGate (fun () ->
                supervisorBuildRequestEpochMs <- Environment.TickCount64
                supervisorBuildRequestEpochMs)

        type TerminalDurableRunEndObservation =
            | TerminalDurableRunEndPending
            | TerminalDurableRunEndObserved

        let mutable private terminalDurableRunEndObservation = TerminalDurableRunEndPending
        let mutable private terminalDurableRunEndIvar = Hopac.IVar<unit>()
        let private terminalDurableRunEndObservedGate = obj()
        let private terminalDurableRunEndObservedNow () =
            lock terminalDurableRunEndObservedGate (fun () ->
                match terminalDurableRunEndObservation with
                | TerminalDurableRunEndObserved -> true
                | TerminalDurableRunEndPending -> false)
        let progressHudTerminalExactNow () = terminalDurableRunEndObservedNow()
        let private terminalDurableRunEndObserveJob () : Hopac.Job<unit> =
            let ivar =
                lock terminalDurableRunEndObservedGate (fun () ->
                    terminalDurableRunEndObservation <- TerminalDurableRunEndObserved
                    terminalDurableRunEndIvar)
            Hopac.IVar.tryFill ivar ()
        // The run-end IVar is filled when the durable writer persists the run-end receipt, but that receipt
        // is only produced after the terminal reducer seals the run, and the seal waits for the committed
        // BuildFile result, which waits here: a cycle that left every BuildFile unanswered. The writer's
        // run-end state is also never reopened for a second request in the same process. Bound the wait:
        // when the receipt has not arrived within the grace period, the result boundary itself is the
        // run end. SPIRAL_RUN_END_GRACE_MS overrides the grace (default 20 ms: the receipt cannot arrive
        // first, so the grace was 500 ms of pure latency at the end of every compile).
        let private terminalRunEndGraceMs =
            match System.Int32.TryParse(System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable "SPIRAL_RUN_END_GRACE_MS") with
            | true, value when value >= 0 -> value
            | _ -> 20
        let awaitTerminalReducerRunEndJob () =
            let ivar = lock terminalDurableRunEndObservedGate (fun () -> terminalDurableRunEndIvar)
            Hopac.Alt.choose [
                Hopac.IVar.read ivar
                Hopac.timeOutMillis terminalRunEndGraceMs |> Hopac.Alt.afterJob (fun () -> terminalDurableRunEndObserveJob ())
            ]
        let private terminalDurableRunEndReset () =
            lock terminalDurableRunEndObservedGate (fun () ->
                terminalDurableRunEndObservation <- TerminalDurableRunEndPending
                terminalDurableRunEndIvar <- Hopac.IVar<unit>())
        let observeTerminalReducerRunEnd () = terminalDurableRunEndObserveJob()
        open System.Globalization
        open System.Diagnostics
        open System.Collections.Generic
        open System.IO
        open System.Text
        open System.Runtime.InteropServices

        type WindowsTaskbarProgressState =
            | NoProgress = 0
            | Indeterminate = 1
            | Normal = 2
            | Error = 4
            | Paused = 8

        type WindowsTaskbarLifecycle =
            | TaskbarRunning
            | TaskbarSucceeded
            | TaskbarFailed of exitCode:int

        type WindowsTaskbarShutdownReason =
            | TaskbarProcessExit of exitCode:int
            | TaskbarCancelKeyPress
            | TaskbarUnhandledException
            | TaskbarExplicitExit of exitCode:int
            | TaskbarPhysicalBoundary of exitCode:int

        type WindowsTaskbarRequestCompletionSource =
            | TaskbarHeartbeatHardAbortBoundary
            | TaskbarBuildFatalBoundary
            | TaskbarBuildErrorBoundary
            | TaskbarRootPromiseFailureBoundary
            | TaskbarNativeClosureFailureBoundary
            | TaskbarTerminalFlowFailureBoundary
            | TaskbarCanonicalRootFailureBoundary
            | TaskbarBuildOkBoundary
            | TaskbarBuildSkipBoundary
            | TaskbarRunEndBoundary
            | TaskbarDurableRunEndBoundary
            | TaskbarDurableTerminalFailureBoundary

        type WindowsTaskbarRequestCompletion =
            | TaskbarRequestSucceeded of source:WindowsTaskbarRequestCompletionSource * exitCode:int
            | TaskbarRequestFailed of source:WindowsTaskbarRequestCompletionSource * exitCode:int

        type WindowsTaskbarShutdownLatch =
            | TaskbarShutdownOpen
            | TaskbarShutdownLatched of WindowsTaskbarShutdownReason

        type WindowsTaskbarInput =
            | TaskbarProgress of percent:float
            | TaskbarRequestCompleted of WindowsTaskbarRequestCompletion
            | TaskbarTerminal of WindowsTaskbarShutdownReason
            | TaskbarIgnore

        type WindowsTaskbarTerminalOutcome =
            | TaskbarTerminalSuccess
            | TaskbarTerminalFailure

        type WindowsTaskbarCreationMode =
            | TaskbarCreationDirectCast
            | TaskbarCreationExplicitQueryInterface

        type WindowsTaskbarInitState =
            | TaskbarInitNotAttempted
            | TaskbarInitUnsupported
            | TaskbarInitHrFailed of hresult:int * mode:WindowsTaskbarCreationMode
            | TaskbarInitReady of hwndCount:int * mode:WindowsTaskbarCreationMode
            | TaskbarInitFaulted of exceptionType:string * hresult:int

        type WindowsTaskbarBackendObservation =
            | TaskbarOscOnly of initState:WindowsTaskbarInitState
            | TaskbarComWindows of hwndCount:int * acceptedCount:int

        type WindowsTaskbarFailureStage =
            | TaskbarShutdownHookUpdate
            | TaskbarTerminalUpdate
            | TaskbarRequestCompletionUpdate
            | TaskbarProgressUpdate

        type WindowsTaskbarPresentationOwner =
            | TaskbarPresentationOwnedInProcess

        type WindowsTaskbarOperationalStatus =
            | TaskbarOperationalUnsupported
            | TaskbarOperationalInit of WindowsTaskbarInitState
            | TaskbarOperationalCleared of exitCode:int * oscAccepted:bool * backend:WindowsTaskbarBackendObservation
            | TaskbarOperationalNormal of permille:int * oscAccepted:bool * backend:WindowsTaskbarBackendObservation
            | TaskbarOperationalShutdownHookCleared of exitCode:int
            | TaskbarOperationalRequestStarted
            | TaskbarOperationalFailed of stage:WindowsTaskbarFailureStage * exceptionType:string * hresult:int
            | TaskbarOperationalNeutralizedByShutdown of prior:WindowsTaskbarOperationalStatus * reason:WindowsTaskbarShutdownReason
            | TaskbarOperationalNeutralizedByRequest of prior:WindowsTaskbarOperationalStatus * completion:WindowsTaskbarRequestCompletion

        let private windowsTaskbarCreationModeText = function
            | TaskbarCreationDirectCast -> "direct_cast"
            | TaskbarCreationExplicitQueryInterface -> "explicit_query_interface"

        let private windowsTaskbarInitStateText = function
            | TaskbarInitNotAttempted -> "not_attempted"
            | TaskbarInitUnsupported -> "unsupported"
            | TaskbarInitHrFailed(hresult, mode) ->
                sprintf "hrinit_failed:0x%08X|mode=%s" hresult (windowsTaskbarCreationModeText mode)
            | TaskbarInitReady(hwndCount, mode) ->
                sprintf "ready:hwnds=%d|mode=%s" hwndCount (windowsTaskbarCreationModeText mode)
            | TaskbarInitFaulted(exceptionType, hresult) ->
                sprintf "init_failed:%s:0x%08X" exceptionType hresult

        let private windowsTaskbarShutdownReasonText = function
            | TaskbarProcessExit exitCode -> sprintf "process_exit:%d" exitCode
            | TaskbarCancelKeyPress -> "cancel_key_press"
            | TaskbarUnhandledException -> "unhandled_exception"
            | TaskbarExplicitExit exitCode -> sprintf "explicit_exit:%d" exitCode
            | TaskbarPhysicalBoundary exitCode -> sprintf "physical_boundary:%d" exitCode

        let private windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionSourceText = function
            | TaskbarHeartbeatHardAbortBoundary -> "heartbeat_hard_abort"
            | TaskbarBuildFatalBoundary -> "build_fatal_error"
            | TaskbarBuildErrorBoundary -> "build_error_trace"
            | TaskbarRootPromiseFailureBoundary -> "root_promise_failed"
            | TaskbarNativeClosureFailureBoundary -> "native_closure_failure"
            | TaskbarTerminalFlowFailureBoundary -> "terminal_flow_typed_failure"
            | TaskbarCanonicalRootFailureBoundary -> "canonical_root_projection_failure"
            | TaskbarBuildOkBoundary -> "build_ok"
            | TaskbarBuildSkipBoundary -> "build_skip"
            | TaskbarRunEndBoundary -> "run_end"
            | TaskbarDurableRunEndBoundary -> "durable_run_end"
            | TaskbarDurableTerminalFailureBoundary -> "durable_terminal_failure"

        let private windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionText = function
            | TaskbarRequestSucceeded(source, exitCode) ->
                sprintf "request_success:%s:%d" (windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionSourceText source) exitCode
            | TaskbarRequestFailed(source, exitCode) ->
                sprintf "request_failure:%s:%d" (windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionSourceText source) exitCode

        let private windowsTaskbarFailureStageText = function
            | TaskbarShutdownHookUpdate -> "shutdown_hook_failed"
            | TaskbarTerminalUpdate -> "terminal_update_failed"
            | TaskbarRequestCompletionUpdate -> "request_completion_failed"
            | TaskbarProgressUpdate -> "update_failed"

        let private windowsTaskbarPresentationOwnerText = function
            | TaskbarPresentationOwnedInProcess -> "disabled:in_process_request_authority"

        let rec private windowsTaskbarOperationalStatusText = function
            | TaskbarOperationalUnsupported -> "unsupported"
            | TaskbarOperationalInit initState -> windowsTaskbarInitStateText initState
            | TaskbarOperationalCleared(exitCode, oscAccepted, TaskbarOscOnly initState) ->
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "cleared|exit=%d|osc=%b|com=%s" [| box exitCode; box oscAccepted; box (windowsTaskbarInitStateText initState) |]
            | TaskbarOperationalCleared(exitCode, oscAccepted, TaskbarComWindows(hwndCount, acceptedCount)) ->
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "cleared|exit=%d|osc=%b|hwnds=%d|accepted=%d" [| box exitCode; box oscAccepted; box hwndCount; box acceptedCount |]
            | TaskbarOperationalNormal(permille, oscAccepted, TaskbarOscOnly initState) ->
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "normal:%d.%d%%|osc=%b|com=%s|authority=determinate_projection_capped_until_dispositive_completion" [| box (permille / 10); box (abs (permille % 10)); box oscAccepted; box (windowsTaskbarInitStateText initState) |]
            | TaskbarOperationalNormal(permille, oscAccepted, TaskbarComWindows(hwndCount, acceptedCount)) ->
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "normal:%d.%d%%|osc=%b|hwnds=%d|accepted=%d|authority=determinate_projection_capped_until_dispositive_completion" [| box (permille / 10); box (abs (permille % 10)); box oscAccepted; box hwndCount; box acceptedCount |]
            | TaskbarOperationalShutdownHookCleared exitCode ->
                sprintf "shutdown_hook_cleared|exit=%d" exitCode
            | TaskbarOperationalRequestStarted ->
                "request_started|authority=supervisor_build_file"
            | TaskbarOperationalFailed(stage, exceptionType, hresult) ->
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "%s:%s:0x%s" [| box (windowsTaskbarFailureStageText stage); box exceptionType; box (sprintf "%08X" hresult) |]
            | TaskbarOperationalNeutralizedByShutdown(prior, reason) ->
                windowsTaskbarOperationalStatusText prior
                + "|neutralization_authority="
                + windowsTaskbarShutdownReasonText reason
            | TaskbarOperationalNeutralizedByRequest(prior, completion) ->
                windowsTaskbarOperationalStatusText prior
                + "|neutralization_authority="
                + windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionText completion

        let private windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionOf (_kind:string) (_eventId:string) =
            // JSON rows are evidence, not request boundaries. run_end is handled only
            // after its own durable append, so the footer can never precede the row
            // that authorizes it.
            None

        let private windowsTaskbarTerminalOutcomeOf (kind:string) (eventId:string) =
            match eventId, kind with
            | _, "native_terminal_exit_contract_physical_boundary"
            | _, "physical_exit_receipt" -> Some TaskbarTerminalSuccess
            | _ -> None

        let private windowsTaskbarSignalIsTerminal kind eventId =
            windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionOf kind eventId |> Option.isSome
            || windowsTaskbarTerminalOutcomeOf kind eventId |> Option.isSome

        [<ComImport>]
        [<Guid("EA1AFB91-9E28-4B86-90E9-9E9F8A5EEA84")>]
        [<InterfaceType(ComInterfaceType.InterfaceIsIUnknown)>]
        type ITaskbarList3 =
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract HrInit : unit -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract AddTab : nativeint -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract DeleteTab : nativeint -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract ActivateTab : nativeint -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract SetActiveAlt : nativeint -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract MarkFullscreenWindow : nativeint * bool -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract SetProgressValue : nativeint * uint64 * uint64 -> int
            [<PreserveSig>]
            abstract SetProgressState : nativeint * WindowsTaskbarProgressState -> int

        [<ComImport>]
        [<Guid("56FDF344-FD6D-11d0-958A-006097C9A090")>]
        [<ClassInterface(ClassInterfaceType.None)>]
        type WindowsTaskbarListClass = class end

        [<DllImport("kernel32.dll")>]
        extern nativeint GetConsoleWindow()

        [<DllImport("kernel32.dll", SetLastError=true)>]
        extern bool AttachConsole(uint32 dwProcessId)

        [<DllImport("user32.dll")>]
        extern nativeint GetForegroundWindow()

        [<DllImport("user32.dll")>]
        extern nativeint GetAncestor(nativeint hwnd, uint32 flags)

        [<DllImport("user32.dll")>]
        extern bool IsWindow(nativeint hwnd)

        let mutable private windowsTaskbar : ITaskbarList3 option = None
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarInitAttempted = false
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarLastPermille = -1
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarStatus = TaskbarOperationalUnsupported
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarInitStatus = TaskbarInitNotAttempted
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarLifecycle = TaskbarRunning
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarShutdownLatch = TaskbarShutdownOpen
        let private windowsTaskbarPresentationOwnerStatus = TaskbarPresentationOwnedInProcess
        let mutable private requestFooterCommit : (unit -> unit) = fun () -> ()
        let mutable private requestFooterReset : (unit -> unit) = fun () -> ()

        type TerminalObserverDrainRequestReason =
            | TerminalObserverDrainProcessExit
            | TerminalObserverDrainSupervisorRequestCompletion
            | TerminalObserverDrainPhysicalBoundary
            | TerminalObserverDrainHostReturn
            | TerminalObserverDrainFailsafe

        let terminalObserverDrainRequestReasonText = function
            | TerminalObserverDrainProcessExit -> "process_exit"
            | TerminalObserverDrainSupervisorRequestCompletion -> "supervisor_request_completion"
            | TerminalObserverDrainPhysicalBoundary -> "physical_boundary"
            | TerminalObserverDrainHostReturn -> "host_return"
            | TerminalObserverDrainFailsafe -> "failsafe"

        let mutable private requestObserverDrain : (TerminalObserverDrainRequestReason -> unit) = fun _ -> ()
        let installObserverDrain handler = requestObserverDrain <- handler

        // Terminal presentation consumes an indexed closure proof.
        // Mutable snapshots may contribute evidence, but they cannot authorize the
        // physical exit or the final JSONL row.  Each constructor advances exactly
        // one phantom stage, making skipped closure obligations unrepresentable.
        type TerminalSemanticDebtClosedStage = class end
        type TerminalPromiseCellsClosedStage = class end
        type TerminalSpecializationWorklistClosedStage = class end
        type TerminalObserverDrainClosedStage = class end
        type TerminalDurableWriterClosedStage = class end
        type TerminalRunEndAuthorizedStage = class end
        type TerminalPhysicalExitAuthorizedStage = class end
        type TerminalFinalRowStage = class end

        [<Struct>]
        type TerminalClosureEvidenceRef = private TerminalClosureEvidenceRef of string

        type private TerminalClosureStageId =
            | TerminalClosureSemanticDebt
            | TerminalClosurePromiseCells
            | TerminalClosureSpecializationWorklist
            | TerminalClosureObserverDrain
            | TerminalClosureDurableWriter
            | TerminalClosureRunEndAuthorization
            | TerminalClosurePhysicalExitAuthorization
            | TerminalClosureFinalRow

        let private terminalClosureStageText = function
            | TerminalClosureSemanticDebt -> "semantic-debt"
            | TerminalClosurePromiseCells -> "promises"
            | TerminalClosureSpecializationWorklist -> "worklist"
            | TerminalClosureObserverDrain -> "observers"
            | TerminalClosureDurableWriter -> "durable-writer"
            | TerminalClosureRunEndAuthorization -> "run-end-authorization"
            | TerminalClosurePhysicalExitAuthorization -> "physical-exit-authorization"
            | TerminalClosureFinalRow -> "final-row"

        let private terminalClosureEvidenceDigest (text:string) =
            use sha256 = System.Security.Cryptography.SHA256.Create()
            let bytes = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes text
            let digest = sha256.ComputeHash bytes
            digest
            |> Array.map (fun value -> value.ToString("x2", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))
            |> String.concat ""

        let terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText text =
            if String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace text then invalidArg "text" "terminal closure evidence must be non-empty"
            TerminalClosureEvidenceRef (terminalClosureEvidenceDigest ("terminal-closure-evidence|" + text))

        let terminalClosureEvidenceRefText (TerminalClosureEvidenceRef evidenceRef) =
            evidenceRef

        type TerminalClosureDisposition =
            | TerminalClosureSuccessful
            | TerminalClosureFailedClosed of failureRef:uint32

        type TerminalClosureSeed = {
            generation : int64
            disposition : TerminalClosureDisposition
            semanticOpenCount : int64
            constitutionRef : uint32
            commitRef : uint32
            doneRef : uint32
            runEndIntentRef : uint32
            physicalExitIntentRef : uint32
            durableWriterRef : uint32
            exitCode : int
        }

        type TerminalClosureSubsystemEvidence =
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemOpen of unresolvedCount:int * evidenceRef:TerminalClosureEvidenceRef
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemClosed of evidenceRef:TerminalClosureEvidenceRef
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemFailedClosedResidual of unresolvedCount:int * evidenceRef:TerminalClosureEvidenceRef

        type TerminalClosureSubsystemSnapshot = {
            promiseCells : TerminalClosureSubsystemEvidence
            specializationWorklist : TerminalClosureSubsystemEvidence
            observerDrain : TerminalClosureSubsystemEvidence
        }

        type private TerminalClosureProofData = {
            seed : TerminalClosureSeed
            promiseClosureRef : TerminalClosureEvidenceRef option
            worklistClosureRef : TerminalClosureEvidenceRef option
            observerDrainRef : TerminalClosureEvidenceRef option
            proofRef : TerminalClosureEvidenceRef
        }

        [<Struct>]
        type TerminalClosureProof<'Stage> = private TerminalClosureProof of TerminalClosureProofData

        type TerminalFinalRowCapability = private {
            proof : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalFinalRowStage>
            capabilityRef : TerminalClosureEvidenceRef
        }

        let private terminalClosureProofData (TerminalClosureProof data) = data

        let private terminalClosureAdvance stage evidenceRef (TerminalClosureProof previous) =
            TerminalClosureProof {
                previous with
                    proofRef =
                        terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText (
                            terminalClosureStageText stage
                            + ":" + terminalClosureEvidenceRefText previous.proofRef
                            + ":" + terminalClosureEvidenceRefText evidenceRef)
            }

        let terminalSemanticDebtClosed seed : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalSemanticDebtClosedStage> option =
            let dispositionText, dispositionValid, semanticDebtAccepted =
                match seed.disposition with
                | TerminalClosureSuccessful ->
                    "successful",
                    seed.exitCode = 0,
                    seed.semanticOpenCount = 0L
                | TerminalClosureFailedClosed failureRef ->
                    "failed-closed:" + string failureRef,
                    failureRef <> 0u && seed.exitCode <> 0,
                    seed.semanticOpenCount = 0L
            if seed.constitutionRef = 0u || seed.commitRef = 0u then None
            elif not dispositionValid || not semanticDebtAccepted then None
            else
                Some (
                    TerminalClosureProof {
                        seed = seed
                        promiseClosureRef = None
                        worklistClosureRef = None
                        observerDrainRef = None
                        proofRef =
                            terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText (
                                terminalClosureStageText TerminalClosureSemanticDebt
                                + ":" + string seed.constitutionRef
                                + "|disposition=" + dispositionText
                                + "|semantic_open=" + string seed.semanticOpenCount)
                    })

        let terminalPromiseCellsClosed
            (snapshot:TerminalClosureSubsystemSnapshot)
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalSemanticDebtClosedStage>)
            : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalPromiseCellsClosedStage> option =
            match snapshot.promiseCells with
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemOpen _ -> None
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemClosed promiseClosureRef
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemFailedClosedResidual(_, promiseClosureRef) ->
                let (TerminalClosureProof data) = terminalClosureAdvance TerminalClosurePromiseCells promiseClosureRef proof
                Some (TerminalClosureProof { data with promiseClosureRef = Some promiseClosureRef })

        let terminalSpecializationWorklistClosed
            (snapshot:TerminalClosureSubsystemSnapshot)
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalPromiseCellsClosedStage>)
            : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalSpecializationWorklistClosedStage> option =
            match snapshot.specializationWorklist with
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemOpen _ -> None
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemClosed worklistClosureRef
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemFailedClosedResidual(_, worklistClosureRef) ->
                let (TerminalClosureProof data) = terminalClosureAdvance TerminalClosureSpecializationWorklist worklistClosureRef proof
                Some (TerminalClosureProof { data with worklistClosureRef = Some worklistClosureRef })

        let terminalObserverDrainClosed
            (snapshot:TerminalClosureSubsystemSnapshot)
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalSpecializationWorklistClosedStage>)
            : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalObserverDrainClosedStage> option =
            match snapshot.observerDrain with
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemOpen _ -> None
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemClosed observerDrainRef
            | TerminalClosureSubsystemFailedClosedResidual(_, observerDrainRef) ->
                let (TerminalClosureProof data) = terminalClosureAdvance TerminalClosureObserverDrain observerDrainRef proof
                Some (TerminalClosureProof { data with observerDrainRef = Some observerDrainRef })

        let terminalDurableWriterClosed
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalObserverDrainClosedStage>)
            : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalDurableWriterClosedStage> option =
            let data = terminalClosureProofData proof
            if data.seed.doneRef = 0u || data.seed.durableWriterRef = 0u then None
            else
                Some (
                    terminalClosureAdvance
                        TerminalClosureDurableWriter
                        (terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText (
                            "done=" + string data.seed.doneRef
                            + "|writer=" + string data.seed.durableWriterRef))
                        proof)

        let terminalRunEndAuthorized
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalDurableWriterClosedStage>)
            : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalRunEndAuthorizedStage> option =
            let data = terminalClosureProofData proof
            if data.seed.runEndIntentRef = 0u then None
            else
                Some (
                    terminalClosureAdvance
                        TerminalClosureRunEndAuthorization
                        (terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText (string data.seed.runEndIntentRef))
                        proof)

        let terminalPhysicalExitAuthorized
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalRunEndAuthorizedStage>)
            : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalPhysicalExitAuthorizedStage> option =
            let data = terminalClosureProofData proof
            if data.seed.physicalExitIntentRef = 0u then None
            else
                Some (
                    terminalClosureAdvance
                        TerminalClosurePhysicalExitAuthorization
                        (terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText (string data.seed.physicalExitIntentRef))
                        proof)

        let terminalFinalRowCapability
            (proof:TerminalClosureProof<TerminalPhysicalExitAuthorizedStage>) =
            let finalProof : TerminalClosureProof<TerminalFinalRowStage> =
                terminalClosureAdvance
                    TerminalClosureFinalRow
                    (terminalClosureEvidenceRefOfText "single-consumer-capability")
                    proof
            let data = terminalClosureProofData finalProof
            { proof = finalProof; capabilityRef = data.proofRef }

        let terminalClosureCapabilityFor seed snapshot =
            terminalSemanticDebtClosed seed
            |> Option.bind (terminalPromiseCellsClosed snapshot)
            |> Option.bind (terminalSpecializationWorklistClosed snapshot)
            |> Option.bind (terminalObserverDrainClosed snapshot)
            |> Option.bind terminalDurableWriterClosed
            |> Option.bind terminalRunEndAuthorized
            |> Option.bind terminalPhysicalExitAuthorized
            |> Option.map terminalFinalRowCapability

        type private TerminalFinalRowCapabilityState =
            | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityMissing
            | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityAvailable of TerminalFinalRowCapability
            | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityConsumed of TerminalFinalRowCapability

        let private terminalFinalRowCapabilityGate = obj()
        let mutable private terminalFinalRowCapabilityState = TerminalFinalRowCapabilityMissing
        let mutable private buildTerminalClosureCapability : (TerminalClosureSeed -> TerminalFinalRowCapability option) = fun _ -> None
        let mutable private resetTerminalClosureCapabilityState : (unit -> unit) = fun () -> ()

        type private TerminalClosureRetryAuthority =
            | TerminalClosureRetryUnavailable
            | TerminalClosureRetryInstalled of retry:(unit -> unit)

        type private TerminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthority =
            | TerminalLedgerHeartbeatUnavailable
            | TerminalLedgerHeartbeatInstalled of heartbeat:(unit -> unit)

        let mutable private terminalClosureRetryAuthority = TerminalClosureRetryUnavailable
        let private terminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthorityGate = obj()
        let mutable private terminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthority = TerminalLedgerHeartbeatUnavailable

        let installTerminalClosureCapabilityBuilder builder =
            buildTerminalClosureCapability <- builder

        let installTerminalClosureReset resetter =
            resetTerminalClosureCapabilityState <- resetter

        let installTerminalClosureRetry retry =
            terminalClosureRetryAuthority <- TerminalClosureRetryInstalled retry

        let installTerminalLedgerHeartbeat heartbeat =
            lock terminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthorityGate (fun () ->
                terminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthority <- TerminalLedgerHeartbeatInstalled heartbeat)

        let retryTerminalClosure () =
            match terminalClosureRetryAuthority with
            | TerminalClosureRetryInstalled retry -> retry ()
            | TerminalClosureRetryUnavailable -> ()

        let invokeTerminalLedgerHeartbeat () =
            let authority =
                lock terminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthorityGate (fun () -> terminalLedgerHeartbeatAuthority)
            match authority with
            | TerminalLedgerHeartbeatInstalled heartbeat -> heartbeat ()
            | TerminalLedgerHeartbeatUnavailable -> ()

        let tryBuildTerminalClosureCapability seed =
            buildTerminalClosureCapability seed

        let publishTerminalClosureCapability capability =
            lock terminalFinalRowCapabilityGate (fun () ->
                match terminalFinalRowCapabilityState with
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityMissing ->
                    terminalFinalRowCapabilityState <- TerminalFinalRowCapabilityAvailable capability
                    capability
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityAvailable existing -> existing
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityConsumed existing -> existing)

        let tryAcquireTerminalFinalRowCapability () =
            lock terminalFinalRowCapabilityGate (fun () ->
                match terminalFinalRowCapabilityState with
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityAvailable capability -> Some capability
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityMissing
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityConsumed _ -> None)

        let commitTerminalFinalRowCapability capability =
            lock terminalFinalRowCapabilityGate (fun () ->
                match terminalFinalRowCapabilityState with
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityAvailable existing when
                    terminalClosureEvidenceRefText existing.capabilityRef
                    = terminalClosureEvidenceRefText capability.capabilityRef ->
                    terminalFinalRowCapabilityState <- TerminalFinalRowCapabilityConsumed existing
                    true
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityMissing
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityAvailable _
                | TerminalFinalRowCapabilityConsumed _ -> false)

        let resetTerminalFinalRowCapability () =
            lock terminalFinalRowCapabilityGate (fun () ->
                terminalFinalRowCapabilityState <- TerminalFinalRowCapabilityMissing)
            try resetTerminalClosureCapabilityState () with _ -> ()

        let terminalFinalRowCapabilityRefText capability =
            terminalClosureEvidenceRefText capability.capabilityRef

        // Taskbar presentation is owned in-process. External helper processes and
        // crash sidecars were migration drift: they introduced a second lifetime,
        // raced the durable writer and could clear green before semantic quiescence.
        let private windowsTaskbarOriginalTitle =
            try Console.Title with _ -> ""
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarWindows : nativeint list = []
        let mutable private windowsTaskbarShutdownHooksInstalled = false
        let private windowsTaskbarGate = obj()

        let taskbarRuntimeStatusNow () =
            lock windowsTaskbarGate (fun () ->
                windowsTaskbarOperationalStatusText windowsTaskbarStatus
                + "|presentation_owner="
                + windowsTaskbarPresentationOwnerText windowsTaskbarPresentationOwnerStatus)

        let private windowsTaskbarCandidateWindows () =
            let consoleWindow = GetConsoleWindow()
            let foregroundWindow = GetForegroundWindow()
            let processWindow =
                try System.Diagnostics.Process.GetCurrentProcess().MainWindowHandle
                with _ -> 0n
            [ consoleWindow
              if consoleWindow <> 0n then GetAncestor(consoleWindow, 2u)
              if consoleWindow <> 0n then GetAncestor(consoleWindow, 3u)
              processWindow
              foregroundWindow ]
            |> List.filter (fun hwnd -> hwnd <> 0n && IsWindow(hwnd))
            |> List.distinct

        let private createWindowsTaskbarInstance (taskbarType:Type) =
            let instance = Activator.CreateInstance(taskbarType)
            try
                (instance :?> ITaskbarList3), TaskbarCreationDirectCast
            with :? InvalidCastException ->
                // Some modern .NET/Windows combinations return an RCW that does not
                // satisfy the F# cast even though the COM object exposes ITaskbarList3.
                // Query the interface explicitly before giving up the COM fallback.
                let unknown = Marshal.GetIUnknownForObject(instance)
                let mutable interfacePointer = 0n
                let mutable interfaceId = typeof<ITaskbarList3>.GUID
                try
                    let queryHr = Marshal.QueryInterface(unknown, &interfaceId, &interfacePointer)
                    if queryHr < 0 || interfacePointer = 0n then Marshal.ThrowExceptionForHR(queryHr)
                    let typedObject = Marshal.GetTypedObjectForIUnknown(interfacePointer, typeof<ITaskbarList3>)
                    (typedObject :?> ITaskbarList3), TaskbarCreationExplicitQueryInterface
                finally
                    if interfacePointer <> 0n then Marshal.Release(interfacePointer) |> ignore
                    Marshal.Release(unknown) |> ignore

        let private tryGetWindowsTaskbar () =
            if Environment.OSVersion.Platform <> PlatformID.Win32NT then
                windowsTaskbarInitStatus <- TaskbarInitUnsupported
                windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalInit windowsTaskbarInitStatus
                None
            elif windowsTaskbarInitAttempted then windowsTaskbar
            else
                windowsTaskbarInitAttempted <- true
                try
                    windowsTaskbarWindows <-
                        windowsTaskbarWindows @ windowsTaskbarCandidateWindows()
                        |> List.filter (fun hwnd -> hwnd <> 0n && IsWindow(hwnd))
                        |> List.distinct
                    let taskbar, creationMode =
                        let taskbarClsid = Guid("56FDF344-FD6D-11d0-958A-006097C9A090")
                        let taskbarType = Type.GetTypeFromCLSID(taskbarClsid)
                        if isNull taskbarType then invalidOp "Windows taskbar COM class is unavailable"
                        createWindowsTaskbarInstance taskbarType
                    let hr = taskbar.HrInit()
                    if hr < 0 then
                        windowsTaskbarInitStatus <- TaskbarInitHrFailed(hr, creationMode)
                        windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalInit windowsTaskbarInitStatus
                        None
                    else
                        windowsTaskbar <- Some taskbar
                        windowsTaskbarInitStatus <- TaskbarInitReady(windowsTaskbarWindows.Length, creationMode)
                        windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalInit windowsTaskbarInitStatus
                        windowsTaskbar
                with ex ->
                    windowsTaskbarInitStatus <- TaskbarInitFaulted(ex.GetType().Name, ex.HResult)
                    windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalInit windowsTaskbarInitStatus
                    None

        let private emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarProgress state progress =
            if Environment.OSVersion.Platform = PlatformID.Win32NT && not Console.IsOutputRedirected then
                try
                    Console.Write(sprintf "\u001b]9;4;%d;%d\u0007" state progress)
                    true
                with _ -> false
            else false

        let private emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarResetForced () =
            if Environment.OSVersion.Platform <> PlatformID.Win32NT then false
            else
                try
                    let payload = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("\u001b]9;4;0;0\u0007")
                    use output = Console.OpenStandardOutput()
                    output.Write(payload, 0, payload.Length)
                    output.Flush()
                    true
                with _ -> emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarProgress 0 0

        let private windowsTaskbarInputOf (kind:string) (eventId:string) (progressText:string) (exitCodeText:string) =
            match windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionOf kind eventId with
            | Some requestCompletion -> TaskbarRequestCompleted requestCompletion
            | None ->
                match windowsTaskbarTerminalOutcomeOf kind eventId with
                | Some terminalOutcome ->
                    let fallbackExitCode =
                        match terminalOutcome with
                        | TaskbarTerminalSuccess -> 0
                        | TaskbarTerminalFailure -> 1
                    let mutable exitCode = fallbackExitCode
                    if not (Int32.TryParse(exitCodeText, &exitCode)) then exitCode <- fallbackExitCode
                    TaskbarTerminal (TaskbarPhysicalBoundary exitCode)
                | None ->
                    let mutable progress = 0.0
                    if Double.TryParse(progressText, NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, &progress) then
                        TaskbarProgress(max 0.0 (min 100.0 progress))
                    else TaskbarIgnore

        let private applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalState exitCode =
            let effectiveExitCode =
                match windowsTaskbarLifecycle, exitCode with
                | TaskbarFailed priorExitCode, 0 -> priorExitCode
                | _, currentExitCode -> currentExitCode
            let failed = effectiveExitCode <> 0
            windowsTaskbarLifecycle <- if failed then TaskbarFailed effectiveExitCode else TaskbarSucceeded
            windowsTaskbarLastPermille <- -1
            let oscAccepted = emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarProgress 0 0
            let forcedOscAccepted = emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarResetForced()
            let oscAccepted = oscAccepted || forcedOscAccepted
            try Console.Title <- windowsTaskbarOriginalTitle with _ -> ()
            if Environment.OSVersion.Platform = PlatformID.Win32NT then
                windowsTaskbarWindows <-
                    windowsTaskbarWindows @ windowsTaskbarCandidateWindows()
                    |> List.filter (fun hwnd -> hwnd <> 0n && IsWindow(hwnd))
                    |> List.distinct
            match tryGetWindowsTaskbar() with
            | None ->
                windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                    TaskbarOperationalCleared(
                        effectiveExitCode,
                        oscAccepted,
                        TaskbarOscOnly windowsTaskbarInitStatus)
            | Some taskbar ->
                windowsTaskbarWindows <- windowsTaskbarWindows |> List.filter (fun hwnd -> hwnd <> 0n && IsWindow(hwnd))
                let mutable accepted = 0
                for hwnd in windowsTaskbarWindows do
                    let stateHr = taskbar.SetProgressState(hwnd, WindowsTaskbarProgressState.NoProgress)
                    if stateHr >= 0 then accepted <- accepted + 1
                windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                    TaskbarOperationalCleared(
                        effectiveExitCode,
                        oscAccepted,
                        TaskbarComWindows(windowsTaskbarWindows.Length, accepted))

        let private windowsTaskbarShutdownExitCode = function
            | TaskbarProcessExit exitCode
            | TaskbarExplicitExit exitCode
            | TaskbarPhysicalBoundary exitCode -> exitCode
            | TaskbarCancelKeyPress -> 130
            | TaskbarUnhandledException -> -1

        let private applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalReason reason =
            let exitCode = windowsTaskbarShutdownExitCode reason
            applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalState exitCode
            windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalNeutralizedByShutdown(windowsTaskbarStatus, reason)

        let private tryApplyWindowsTaskbarShutdownReason reason =
            let exitCode = windowsTaskbarShutdownExitCode reason
            windowsTaskbarShutdownLatch <- TaskbarShutdownLatched reason
            let mutable lockTaken = false
            try
                try
                    System.Threading.Monitor.TryEnter(windowsTaskbarGate, 250, &lockTaken)
                    if lockTaken then
                        applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalReason reason
                    else
                        emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarProgress 0 0 |> ignore
                        emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarResetForced() |> ignore
                        try Console.Title <- windowsTaskbarOriginalTitle with _ -> ()
                        windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalShutdownHookCleared exitCode
                with ex ->
                    windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalFailed(TaskbarShutdownHookUpdate, ex.GetType().Name, ex.HResult)
            finally
                if lockTaken then System.Threading.Monitor.Exit(windowsTaskbarGate)

        let private installWindowsTaskbarShutdownHooks () =
            let shouldInstall =
                lock windowsTaskbarGate (fun () ->
                    if windowsTaskbarShutdownHooksInstalled then false
                    else
                        windowsTaskbarShutdownHooksInstalled <- true
                        true)
            if shouldInstall then
                AppDomain.CurrentDomain.ProcessExit.Add(fun _ ->
                    tryApplyWindowsTaskbarShutdownReason (TaskbarProcessExit Environment.ExitCode))
                AppDomain.CurrentDomain.UnhandledException.Add(fun _ ->
                    tryApplyWindowsTaskbarShutdownReason TaskbarUnhandledException)
                try
                    Console.CancelKeyPress.Add(fun _ ->
                        tryApplyWindowsTaskbarShutdownReason TaskbarCancelKeyPress)
                with _ -> ()

        let private windowsTaskbarRequestRestartThreshold = 5.0
        let private windowsTaskbarProvisionalCompletionCeiling = 99.9

        let private applyWindowsTaskbarProgress bounded =
            // A projected percentage is presentation only.  Keep the request in
            // determinate Normal mode so Windows can fill the bar, but cap a live
            // 100% projection below completion.  Only a dispositive request or
            // process boundary may neutralize the taskbar.
            let acceptsProgress =
                match windowsTaskbarShutdownLatch with
                | TaskbarShutdownLatched _ -> false
                | TaskbarShutdownOpen ->
                    match windowsTaskbarLifecycle with
                    | TaskbarRunning -> true
                    | TaskbarSucceeded when bounded <= windowsTaskbarRequestRestartThreshold ->
                        terminalDurableRunEndReset ()
                        windowsTaskbarLifecycle <- TaskbarRunning
                        windowsTaskbarLastPermille <- -1
                        true
                    | TaskbarFailed _ when bounded <= windowsTaskbarRequestRestartThreshold ->
                        terminalDurableRunEndReset ()
                        windowsTaskbarLifecycle <- TaskbarRunning
                        windowsTaskbarLastPermille <- -1
                        true
                    | _ -> false
            if acceptsProgress then
                let boundedForPaint =
                    if bounded >= 100.0 then windowsTaskbarProvisionalCompletionCeiling
                    else max 0.0 bounded
                let permille = int (Math.Round(boundedForPaint * 10.0))
                if windowsTaskbarLastPermille < 0 || abs (permille - windowsTaskbarLastPermille) >= 5 then
                    windowsTaskbarLastPermille <- permille
                    let oscPercent = max 0 (min 99 (int (Math.Floor boundedForPaint)))
                    let oscAccepted = emitWindowsTerminalTaskbarProgress 1 oscPercent
                    try Console.Title <- sprintf "Spiral compile %.1f%%" boundedForPaint with _ -> ()
                    let taskbar = tryGetWindowsTaskbar()
                    match taskbar with
                    | None ->
                        windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                            TaskbarOperationalNormal(
                                permille,
                                oscAccepted,
                                TaskbarOscOnly windowsTaskbarInitStatus)
                    | Some taskbar ->
                        windowsTaskbarWindows <- windowsTaskbarWindows |> List.filter (fun hwnd -> hwnd <> 0n && IsWindow(hwnd))
                        let mutable accepted = 0
                        for hwnd in windowsTaskbarWindows do
                            let stateHr = taskbar.SetProgressState(hwnd, WindowsTaskbarProgressState.Normal)
                            let valueHr = taskbar.SetProgressValue(hwnd, uint64 permille, 1000UL)
                            if stateHr >= 0 && valueHr >= 0 then accepted <- accepted + 1
                        windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                            TaskbarOperationalNormal(
                                permille,
                                oscAccepted,
                                TaskbarComWindows(windowsTaskbarWindows.Length, accepted))
            match windowsTaskbarShutdownLatch with
            | TaskbarShutdownLatched reason when acceptsProgress ->
                applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalReason reason
            | _ -> ()

        let private completeWindowsTaskbarForReason reason =
            installWindowsTaskbarShutdownHooks()
            // Process/physical-boundary presentation shares the bounded shutdown
            // path. Taskbar ownership is never terminal authority and therefore
            // cannot hold process exit behind an unbounded UI lock.
            tryApplyWindowsTaskbarShutdownReason reason

        let private windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionExitCode = function
            | TaskbarRequestSucceeded(_, exitCode)
            | TaskbarRequestFailed(_, exitCode) -> exitCode

        let private applyWindowsTaskbarRequestCompletion completion =
            // A build boundary clears presentation but deliberately leaves the
            // process shutdown latch open so the next request can paint again.
            let exitCode = windowsTaskbarRequestCompletionExitCode completion
            applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalState exitCode
            windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                TaskbarOperationalNeutralizedByRequest(windowsTaskbarStatus, completion)

        let private completeWindowsTaskbarForRequest completion =
            installWindowsTaskbarShutdownHooks()
            let mutable lockTaken = false
            try
                System.Threading.Monitor.TryEnter(windowsTaskbarGate, 250, &lockTaken)
                if lockTaken then
                    try applyWindowsTaskbarRequestCompletion completion
                    with ex ->
                        windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                            TaskbarOperationalFailed(TaskbarRequestCompletionUpdate, ex.GetType().Name, ex.HResult)
                else
                    // Request-completion presentation is observer-only. A stuck UI owner
                    // must never hold a durable terminal closure after its receipts commit.
                    windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                        TaskbarOperationalFailed(TaskbarRequestCompletionUpdate, "TaskbarRequestGateTimeout", 0)
            finally
                if lockTaken then System.Threading.Monitor.Exit(windowsTaskbarGate)

        let private completeWindowsTaskbarForExit exitCode =
            completeWindowsTaskbarForReason (TaskbarExplicitExit exitCode)

        let private completeWindowsTaskbarForDurableRunEnd exitCode =
            completeWindowsTaskbarForRequest (TaskbarRequestSucceeded(TaskbarDurableRunEndBoundary, exitCode))

        let private completeWindowsTaskbarForDurableTerminalFailure exitCode =
            completeWindowsTaskbarForRequest (TaskbarRequestFailed(TaskbarDurableTerminalFailureBoundary, exitCode))

        // The supervisor is a long-lived server. These request-boundary functions
        // clear presentation exactly when the BuildFile response is committed to
        // its IVar, without latching process shutdown or waiting for process exit.
        let beginSupervisorBuildRequest () =
            installWindowsTaskbarShutdownHooks()
            let _requestEpochMs = advanceSupervisorBuildRequestEpoch ()
            // Request-scoped completion authority must reset independently of any
            // process/taskbar shutdown latch carried by the long-lived Supervisor.
            terminalDurableRunEndReset ()
            requestFooterReset ()
            lock windowsTaskbarGate (fun () ->
                match windowsTaskbarShutdownLatch with
                | TaskbarShutdownLatched _ -> ()
                | TaskbarShutdownOpen ->
                    windowsTaskbarLifecycle <- TaskbarRunning
                    windowsTaskbarLastPermille <- -1
                    windowsTaskbarStatus <- TaskbarOperationalRequestStarted)

        let completeSupervisorBuildRequestSucceeded () =
            completeWindowsTaskbarForRequest (TaskbarRequestSucceeded(TaskbarBuildOkBoundary, 0))
            requestFooterCommit ()

        let completeSupervisorBuildRequestFailed () =
            completeWindowsTaskbarForRequest (TaskbarRequestFailed(TaskbarBuildErrorBoundary, 1))
            requestFooterCommit ()

        let completeSupervisorBuildRequestSkipped () =
            completeWindowsTaskbarForRequest (TaskbarRequestSucceeded(TaskbarBuildSkipBoundary, 0))
            requestFooterCommit ()

        let private updateWindowsTaskbarProgress (kind:string) (eventId:string) (progressText:string) (exitCodeText:string) =
            installWindowsTaskbarShutdownHooks()
            lock windowsTaskbarGate (fun () ->
                try
                    match windowsTaskbarInputOf kind eventId progressText exitCodeText with
                    | TaskbarRequestCompleted completion -> applyWindowsTaskbarRequestCompletion completion
                    | TaskbarTerminal reason ->
                        windowsTaskbarShutdownLatch <- TaskbarShutdownLatched reason
                        applyWindowsTaskbarTerminalReason reason
                    | TaskbarProgress bounded -> applyWindowsTaskbarProgress bounded
                    | TaskbarIgnore -> ()
                with ex ->
                    windowsTaskbarStatus <-
                        TaskbarOperationalFailed(TaskbarProgressUpdate, ex.GetType().Name, ex.HResult))

        let private gate = obj()

        // MIGRATION destructive migration : the HUD no longer rebuilds authority
        // by reparsing whatever JSON line happened to arrive last. The reducer publishes
        // one coherent typed snapshot; the painter is an observer of that immutable value.
        type ReducerHudProgressPhase =
            | ReducerHudDiscovering
            | ReducerHudMaterial
            | ReducerHudTopologyPause
            | ReducerHudRescue
            | ReducerHudTerminalizing
            | ReducerHudComplete

        type ReducerHudDiscoveryState =
            | ReducerHudDiscoveryOpen of reserveCost:int64
            | ReducerHudDiscoveryClosed

        type ReducerHudPossessionStage =
            | ReducerHudPossessionVacant
            | ReducerHudPossessionArmed
            | ReducerHudPossessionFilled
            | ReducerHudPossessionWriterBound
            | ReducerHudPossessionArtifactsCommitted
            | ReducerHudPossessionExitWitnessQueued
            | ReducerHudPossessionSealed
            | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed

        type ReducerHudOutcomeId =
            | ReducerHudOutcomeOpen
            | ReducerHudOutcomeSuccessful
            | ReducerHudOutcomeFailedClosed

        type ReducerHudBlocker =
            | ReducerHudOwnerClosure
            | ReducerHudWorkDagClosure
            | ReducerHudSchedulerCausality
            | ReducerHudSemanticFactDebt
            | ReducerHudCrossKindObligation
            | ReducerHudSidecarDrain
            | ReducerHudContinuationCell
            | ReducerHudKnownWork

        type ReducerHudFinalBlockerCountAuthority =
            | ReducerHudFinalBlockerRows
            | ReducerHudFinalTerminalProtocolResidual
            | ReducerHudFinalNoBlocker

        type ReducerHudFinalExactDenominatorAuthority =
            | ReducerHudFinalSemanticGapExact
            | ReducerHudFinalSemanticGapInexact

        type ReducerHudCrossKindState =
            | ReducerHudCrossKindClear
            | ReducerHudCrossKindLive of obligationCount:int64

        type ReducerHudCyclePoisonState =
            | ReducerHudCyclePoisonClear
            | ReducerHudCyclePoisonSuspected of repeatCount:int64
            | ReducerHudCyclePoisonQuarantined of receiptRef:uint32

        type ReducerHudHotNode =
            | ReducerHudHotNodeUnknown
            | ReducerHudHotNodeKnown of nodeId:string * sourcePath:string * sourceLine:int * nodeKind:string * queueDepth:int64

        type ReducerHudRateSnapshot = {
            phase : ReducerHudProgressPhase
            shortSemanticCostPerSecond : float
            mediumSemanticCostPerSecond : float
            sessionSemanticCostPerSecond : float
            fusedSemanticCostPerSecond : float
            variance : float
            confidence : float
            samples : int64
            rateAuthorityRef : string
        }

        type ReducerHudAstWorkSnapshot = {
            completedCost : int64
            discoveredCost : int64
            totalCost : int64
            exact : bool
            sourceRef : string
        }

        type ReducerHudSemanticWorkSnapshot = {
            retiredCost : int64
            discoveredCost : int64
            knownRemainingCost : int64
            blockedCost : int64
            provenDeadCost : int64
            reserveP50Cost : int64
            reserveP90Cost : int64
            totalLow : int64
            totalMid : int64
            totalHigh : int64
            exact : bool
            revision : int64
        }

        type ReducerHudWorkSnapshot = {
            ast : ReducerHudAstWorkSnapshot
            semantic : ReducerHudSemanticWorkSnapshot
            lowBp : int64
            midBp : int64
            highBp : int64
        }

        type ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonKind private () =
            static member InternedKindTag () = 0x120001u

        type ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonId =
            CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId<ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonKind>

        module ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonIdOps =
            let create value : ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonId =
                CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId.create<ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonKind> value
            let text (value:ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonId) =
                CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId.text value

        type ReducerHudCpuAuthority =
            | ReducerHudCpuUnavailable of reason:ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonId
            | ReducerHudCpuExclusiveWorker of workerRef:string

        let reducerHudCpuAuthorityText = function
            | ReducerHudCpuUnavailable reason -> "unavailable:" + ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonIdOps.text reason
            | ReducerHudCpuExclusiveWorker workerRef -> "exclusive_worker:" + workerRef

        type ReducerHudTimingSnapshot = {
            cpuExclusiveMs : int64 option
            cpuAuthority : ReducerHudCpuAuthority
            wallInclusiveMs : int64
            queueDelayMs : int64
            blockedOnChildMs : int64
            timingReceiptRef : string
        }

        type ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonKind private () =
            static member InternedKindTag () = 0x120002u

        type ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonId =
            CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId<ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonKind>

        module ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonIdOps =
            let create value : ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonId =
                CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId.create<ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonKind> value
            let text (value:ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonId) =
                CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId.text value

        type ReducerHudCriticalPathState =
            | ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknown of reason:ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonId
            | ReducerHudCriticalPathSemanticRemaining of cost:int64 * authorityRef:string

        let reducerHudCriticalPathRemainingCost = function
            | ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknown _ -> None
            | ReducerHudCriticalPathSemanticRemaining(cost, _) -> Some(max 0L cost)

        let reducerHudCriticalPathText = function
            | ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknown reason -> "unknown:" + ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonIdOps.text reason
            | ReducerHudCriticalPathSemanticRemaining(cost, authorityRef) ->
                "semantic_remaining=" + string (max 0L cost) + "|authority=" + authorityRef

        type ReducerHudEtaSnapshot = {
            phase : ReducerHudProgressPhase
            terminalP50Ms : int64 option
            terminalP90Ms : int64 option
            confidenceSigmaMs : int64 option
            criticalPath : ReducerHudCriticalPathState
            effectiveParallelism : float
            rateAuthorityRef : string
        }

        type ReducerHudQapStageId =
            | ReducerHudQapUnknown
            | ReducerHudQapAwaiting
            | ReducerHudQapProgressing
            | ReducerHudQapDrained
            | ReducerHudQapDeadlocked

        let reducerHudQapStageText = function
            | ReducerHudQapUnknown -> ""
            | ReducerHudQapAwaiting -> "QapAwaiting"
            | ReducerHudQapProgressing -> "QapProgressing"
            | ReducerHudQapDrained -> "QapDrained"
            | ReducerHudQapDeadlocked -> "QapDeadlocked"

        type ReducerHudSnapshot = {
            generation : int64
            snapshotMs : int64
            elapsedMsAtSnapshot : int64
            phase : ReducerHudProgressPhase
            discovery : ReducerHudDiscoveryState
            work : ReducerHudWorkSnapshot
            rates : ReducerHudRateSnapshot
            timing : ReducerHudTimingSnapshot
            eta : ReducerHudEtaSnapshot
            possession : ReducerHudPossessionStage
            actorRef : string
            stageTokenRef : string
            fillReceiptRef : string
            runEndReceiptRef : string
            physicalExitReceiptRef : string
            terminalSnapshotRef : string
            operationalRevision : int64
            operationalGraphRef : string
            runtimeAuthorityRef : string
            semanticEpoch : int64
            qapGenerationRef : string
            qapStage : ReducerHudQapStageId
            commitReceiptRef : string
            doneReceiptRef : string
            exitCode : int option
            sealedAtMs : int64 option
            blockers : ReducerHudBlocker list
            hotNode : ReducerHudHotNode
            crossKind : ReducerHudCrossKindState
            cyclePoison : ReducerHudCyclePoisonState
        }

        let reducerHudEtaP50Ms (snapshot:ReducerHudSnapshot) = snapshot.eta.terminalP50Ms |> Option.defaultValue -1L
        let reducerHudEtaP90Ms (snapshot:ReducerHudSnapshot) = snapshot.eta.terminalP90Ms |> Option.defaultValue -1L
        let reducerHudEtaSigmaMs (snapshot:ReducerHudSnapshot) = snapshot.eta.confidenceSigmaMs |> Option.defaultValue -1L
        let reducerHudEtaP50Seconds snapshot =
            let value = reducerHudEtaP50Ms snapshot
            if value < 0L then -1L else value / 1000L
        let reducerHudEtaP90Seconds snapshot =
            let value = reducerHudEtaP90Ms snapshot
            if value < 0L then -1L else value / 1000L
        let reducerHudEtaSigmaSeconds snapshot =
            let value = reducerHudEtaSigmaMs snapshot
            if value < 0L then -1L else value / 1000L

        type ReducerHudSnapshotAdvance =
            | ReducerHudSnapshotInstalled of generation:int64
            | ReducerHudSnapshotIdempotent of generation:int64
            | ReducerHudSnapshotRejectedRegression of currentGeneration:int64 * attemptedGeneration:int64

        open Hopac

        // Bonus migration : the authoritative HUD snapshot is actor-owned.
        // No lock or mutable cell can publish a mixed generation.  JSON and the
        // visible painter are read-only consumers of this mailbox.
        type ReducerHudMailboxMessage =
            | ReducerHudPublishTerminalBlockers of ReducerHudBlocker list * IVar<unit>
            | ReducerHudPublishSnapshot of ReducerHudSnapshot * IVar<ReducerHudSnapshotAdvance>
            | ReducerHudPublishSnapshotNoReply of ReducerHudSnapshot
            | ReducerHudReadSnapshot of IVar<ReducerHudSnapshot option>

        type ReducerHudMailboxState = private {
            snapshot : ReducerHudSnapshot option
            terminalBlockers : ReducerHudBlocker list
        }

        // MIGRATION: the mailbox remains the only writer, while visual/cancel
        // observers consume an immutable projection mirror.  This deliberately
        // forbids Hopac.run from paint and shutdown paths, avoiding nested-run
        // scheduler deadlock without giving the mirror mutation authority.
        let private reducerHudProjectionGate = obj()
        let private reducerHudBootstrapSnapshot () : ReducerHudSnapshot =
            { generation = 0L
              snapshotMs = System.DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds()
              elapsedMsAtSnapshot = 0L
              phase = ReducerHudDiscovering
              discovery = ReducerHudDiscoveryOpen 0L
              work =
                { ast =
                    { completedCost = 0L
                      discoveredCost = 0L
                      totalCost = 0L
                      exact = false
                      sourceRef = "" }
                  semantic =
                    { retiredCost = 0L
                      discoveredCost = 0L
                      knownRemainingCost = 0L
                      blockedCost = 0L
                      provenDeadCost = 0L
                      reserveP50Cost = 0L
                      reserveP90Cost = 0L
                      totalLow = 0L
                      totalMid = 0L
                      totalHigh = 0L
                      exact = false
                      revision = 0L }
                  lowBp = 0L
                  midBp = 0L
                  highBp = 0L }
              rates =
                { phase = ReducerHudDiscovering
                  shortSemanticCostPerSecond = 0.0
                  mediumSemanticCostPerSecond = 0.0
                  sessionSemanticCostPerSecond = 0.0
                  fusedSemanticCostPerSecond = 0.0
                  variance = 0.0
                  confidence = 0.0
                  samples = 0L
                  rateAuthorityRef = "" }
              timing =
                { cpuExclusiveMs = None
                  cpuAuthority = ReducerHudCpuUnavailable (ReducerHudCpuUnavailableReasonIdOps.create "bootstrap")
                  wallInclusiveMs = 0L
                  queueDelayMs = 0L
                  blockedOnChildMs = 0L
                  timingReceiptRef = "" }
              eta =
                { phase = ReducerHudDiscovering
                  terminalP50Ms = None
                  terminalP90Ms = None
                  confidenceSigmaMs = None
                  criticalPath = ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknown (ReducerHudCriticalPathUnknownReasonIdOps.create "bootstrap")
                  effectiveParallelism = 1.0
                  rateAuthorityRef = "" }
              possession = ReducerHudPossessionVacant
              actorRef = ""
              stageTokenRef = ""
              fillReceiptRef = ""
              runEndReceiptRef = ""
              physicalExitReceiptRef = ""
              terminalSnapshotRef = ""
              operationalRevision = 0L
              operationalGraphRef = ""
              runtimeAuthorityRef = ""
              semanticEpoch = 0L
              qapGenerationRef = ""
              qapStage = ReducerHudQapAwaiting
              commitReceiptRef = ""
              doneReceiptRef = ""
              exitCode = None
              sealedAtMs = None
              blockers = [ReducerHudKnownWork]
              hotNode = ReducerHudHotNodeUnknown
              crossKind = ReducerHudCrossKindClear
              cyclePoison = ReducerHudCyclePoisonClear }
        let mutable private reducerHudProjection : ReducerHudSnapshot option =
            Some (reducerHudBootstrapSnapshot())
        let private installReducerHudProjection snapshot blockers =
            let projected = { snapshot with blockers = (snapshot.blockers @ blockers) |> List.distinct }
            lock reducerHudProjectionGate (fun () -> reducerHudProjection <- Some projected)
            // Taskbar projection changes only when a new immutable reducer snapshot is
            // installed. The 20 FPS clock painter must remain a pure console observer.
            let progressPct =
                if projected.work.semantic.totalMid <= 0L then 0.0
                else 100.0 * float projected.work.semantic.retiredCost / float projected.work.semantic.totalMid
            updateWindowsTaskbarProgress
                "reducer_hud_snapshot"
                ""
                (progressPct.ToString("F6", Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))
                ""
        let private readReducerHudProjection () =
            lock reducerHudProjectionGate (fun () -> reducerHudProjection)

        let private reducerHudMailbox = Ch<ReducerHudMailboxMessage>()

        let private reducerHudPhaseRank = function
            | ReducerHudDiscovering -> 0
            | ReducerHudMaterial -> 1
            | ReducerHudTopologyPause -> 2
            | ReducerHudRescue -> 3
            | ReducerHudTerminalizing -> 4
            | ReducerHudComplete -> 5

        let private reducerHudPossessionRank = function
            | ReducerHudPossessionVacant -> 0
            | ReducerHudPossessionArmed -> 1
            | ReducerHudPossessionFilled -> 2
            | ReducerHudPossessionWriterBound -> 3
            | ReducerHudPossessionArtifactsCommitted -> 4
            | ReducerHudPossessionExitWitnessQueued -> 5
            | ReducerHudPossessionSealed -> 6
            | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed -> 6

        let private reducerHudSnapshotRegresses (current:ReducerHudSnapshot) (incoming:ReducerHudSnapshot) =
            incoming.generation = current.generation
            && (reducerHudPhaseRank incoming.phase < reducerHudPhaseRank current.phase
                || incoming.work.midBp < current.work.midBp
                || reducerHudPossessionRank incoming.possession < reducerHudPossessionRank current.possession)

        let rec private reducerHudMailboxLoop (state:ReducerHudMailboxState) =
            job {
                let! message = Ch.take reducerHudMailbox
                match message with
                | ReducerHudPublishTerminalBlockers(blockers, reply) ->
                    let next = { state with terminalBlockers = blockers |> List.distinct }
                    match next.snapshot with
                    | Some snapshot -> installReducerHudProjection snapshot next.terminalBlockers
                    | None -> ()
                    do! IVar.fill reply ()
                    return! reducerHudMailboxLoop next
                | ReducerHudPublishSnapshot(snapshot, reply) ->
                    match state.snapshot with
                    | Some current when snapshot.generation < current.generation ->
                        do! IVar.fill reply (ReducerHudSnapshotRejectedRegression(current.generation, snapshot.generation))
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
                    | Some current when reducerHudSnapshotRegresses current snapshot ->
                        do! IVar.fill reply (ReducerHudSnapshotRejectedRegression(current.generation, snapshot.generation))
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
                    | Some current when snapshot.generation = current.generation && snapshot = current ->
                        do! IVar.fill reply (ReducerHudSnapshotIdempotent snapshot.generation)
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
                    | _ ->
                        let next = { state with snapshot = Some snapshot }
                        installReducerHudProjection snapshot next.terminalBlockers
                        do! IVar.fill reply (ReducerHudSnapshotInstalled snapshot.generation)
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop next
                | ReducerHudPublishSnapshotNoReply snapshot ->
                    match state.snapshot with
                    | Some current when snapshot.generation < current.generation ->
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
                    | Some current when reducerHudSnapshotRegresses current snapshot ->
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
                    | Some current when snapshot.generation = current.generation && snapshot = current ->
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
                    | _ ->
                        let next = { state with snapshot = Some snapshot }
                        installReducerHudProjection snapshot next.terminalBlockers
                        return! reducerHudMailboxLoop next
                | ReducerHudReadSnapshot reply ->
                    let projected =
                        state.snapshot
                        |> Option.map (fun snapshot ->
                            { snapshot with blockers = (snapshot.blockers @ state.terminalBlockers) |> List.distinct })
                    do! IVar.fill reply projected
                    return! reducerHudMailboxLoop state
            }

        let private reducerHudMailboxStarted =
            lazy (
                let bootstrap = reducerHudBootstrapSnapshot()
                installReducerHudProjection bootstrap []
                startHopacJob (reducerHudMailboxLoop { snapshot = Some bootstrap; terminalBlockers = [] }))

        let private ensureReducerHudMailboxStarted () =
            CompilerRuntimeActivation.requireInProcessEntered "reducer_hud_mailbox"
            reducerHudMailboxStarted.Force()

        let publishReducerHudTerminalBlockers (blockers:ReducerHudBlocker list) =
            ensureReducerHudMailboxStarted()
            // Fire-and-ack in the actor lane. Callers never block a Hopac worker
            // by starting a nested scheduler run merely to update a visual projection.
            startHopacJob (job {
                let reply = IVar<unit>()
                do! Ch.send reducerHudMailbox (ReducerHudPublishTerminalBlockers(blockers, reply))
                do! IVar.read reply
            })


        let publishReducerHudSnapshot (snapshot:ReducerHudSnapshot) =
            ensureReducerHudMailboxStarted()
            startHopacJob (job {
                do! Ch.send reducerHudMailbox (ReducerHudPublishSnapshotNoReply snapshot)
            })

        let readReducerHudSnapshot () =
            ensureReducerHudMailboxStarted()
            // Projection-only and bounded: safe from Hopac jobs, Ctrl+C handlers,
            // final HUD persistence and ordinary compiler threads.
            readReducerHudProjection ()

        let private reducerHudProgressPhaseText = function
            | ReducerHudDiscovering -> "discovering"
            | ReducerHudMaterial -> "material"
            | ReducerHudTopologyPause -> "topology_pause"
            | ReducerHudRescue -> "rescue"
            | ReducerHudTerminalizing -> "terminalizing"
            | ReducerHudComplete -> "complete"

        let private reducerHudPossessionText = function
            | ReducerHudPossessionVacant -> "vacant"
            | ReducerHudPossessionArmed -> "armed"
            | ReducerHudPossessionFilled -> "filled"
            | ReducerHudPossessionWriterBound -> "writer_bound"
            | ReducerHudPossessionArtifactsCommitted -> "artifacts_committed"
            | ReducerHudPossessionExitWitnessQueued -> "exit_witness_queued"
            | ReducerHudPossessionSealed -> "sealed"
            | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed -> "failed_closed"

        let private reducerHudOutcomeId runEndObserved exitCode =
            match exitCode with
            | Some code when code <> 0 -> ReducerHudOutcomeFailedClosed
            | Some 0 when runEndObserved -> ReducerHudOutcomeSuccessful
            // A durable run_end proves closure ordering, not success by itself. A
            // failed-closed chain may publish run_end before its exit-code overlay is
            // physically authoritative; keep that projection Open rather than green.
            | _ -> ReducerHudOutcomeOpen

        let private reducerHudOutcomeText = function
            | ReducerHudOutcomeOpen -> "Open"
            | ReducerHudOutcomeSuccessful -> "Successful"
            | ReducerHudOutcomeFailedClosed -> "FailedClosed"

        let private reducerHudOutcomeIsFailedClosed = function
            | ReducerHudOutcomeFailedClosed -> true
            | ReducerHudOutcomeOpen
            | ReducerHudOutcomeSuccessful -> false

        let private reducerHudBlockerText = function
            | ReducerHudOwnerClosure -> "owner_closure"
            | ReducerHudWorkDagClosure -> "work_dag_closure"
            | ReducerHudSchedulerCausality -> "scheduler_causality"
            | ReducerHudSemanticFactDebt -> "semantic_fact_debt"
            | ReducerHudCrossKindObligation -> "cross_kind"
            | ReducerHudSidecarDrain -> "sidecar"
            | ReducerHudContinuationCell -> "continuation"
            | ReducerHudKnownWork -> "known_work"

        let private reducerHudFinalBlockerCountAuthorityText = function
            | ReducerHudFinalBlockerRows -> "SnapshotBlockerRows"
            | ReducerHudFinalTerminalProtocolResidual -> "TerminalProtocolResidual"
            | ReducerHudFinalNoBlocker -> "NoBlocker"

        let private reducerHudFinalExactDenominatorAuthorityText = function
            | ReducerHudFinalSemanticGapExact -> "SemanticGapProjectionExact"
            | ReducerHudFinalSemanticGapInexact -> "SemanticGapProjectionInexact"

        let private reducerHudNextActionText (snapshot:ReducerHudSnapshot) =
            match snapshot.possession with
            | ReducerHudPossessionSealed -> "physical_exit_complete"
            | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed -> "physical_exit_failed_closed"
            | ReducerHudPossessionExitWitnessQueued -> "await_physical_exit_boundary"
            | ReducerHudPossessionArtifactsCommitted -> "queue_exit_witness"
            | ReducerHudPossessionWriterBound -> "commit_artifacts"
            | ReducerHudPossessionFilled -> "bind_writer_capability"
            | ReducerHudPossessionArmed -> "fill_terminal_outcome"
            | ReducerHudPossessionVacant when List.isEmpty snapshot.blockers -> "advance_terminal_protocol"
            | ReducerHudPossessionVacant -> "retire_typed_blockers"

        let private reducerHudLines nowMs (snapshot:ReducerHudSnapshot) =
            let ageMs = max 0L (nowMs - snapshot.snapshotMs)
            let elapsedMs = max 0L (snapshot.elapsedMsAtSnapshot + ageMs)
            let etaMillisecondsKnown value = value >= 0L
            let etaMillisecondsText value =
                if etaMillisecondsKnown value then sprintf "%.3fs" (float value / 1000.0)
                else "unavailable"
            let etaP50AtSnapshotMs = reducerHudEtaP50Ms snapshot
            let etaMs =
                if etaMillisecondsKnown etaP50AtSnapshotMs then max 0L (etaP50AtSnapshotMs - ageMs)
                else -1L
            let outcomeId =
                match snapshot.possession with
                | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed -> ReducerHudOutcomeFailedClosed
                | _ -> reducerHudOutcomeId (not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.runEndReceiptRef)) snapshot.exitCode
            let failedClosed = reducerHudOutcomeIsFailedClosed outcomeId
            let terminalProtocolOpen =
                outcomeId = ReducerHudOutcomeOpen
                && snapshot.phase = ReducerHudTerminalizing
                && (match snapshot.possession with
                    | ReducerHudPossessionSealed
                    | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed -> false
                    | _ -> true)
            let etaText =
                if failedClosed then "failed_closed"
                elif terminalProtocolOpen then "terminal_protocol_open"
                elif etaMs < 0L then "unavailable"
                else sprintf "%.3fs" (float etaMs / 1000.0)
            let elapsedText = sprintf "%.3fs" (float elapsedMs / 1000.0)
            let totalText =
                if failedClosed then "failed_closed"
                elif terminalProtocolOpen then "terminal_protocol_open"
                elif etaMs < 0L then "unavailable"
                else sprintf "%.3fs" (float (elapsedMs + etaMs) / 1000.0)
            let compileProgressPctRaw = if snapshot.work.semantic.totalMid <= 0L then 0.0 else 100.0 * float snapshot.work.semantic.retiredCost / float snapshot.work.semantic.totalMid
            let compileProgressPct = compileProgressPctRaw
            let terminalProgressPct =
                if failedClosed then
                    match snapshot.possession with
                    | ReducerHudPossessionFailedClosed
                    | ReducerHudPossessionSealed -> 100.0
                    | _ -> min 99.0 (max compileProgressPct (float snapshot.work.midBp / 100.0))
                else
                    match snapshot.phase with
                    | ReducerHudComplete -> 100.0
                    | _ -> min 99.0 (max compileProgressPct (float snapshot.work.midBp / 100.0))
            let outcomeLabel =
                match outcomeId with
                | ReducerHudOutcomeFailedClosed -> "FAILED"
                | ReducerHudOutcomeSuccessful -> "SPIRAL SOTA"
                | ReducerHudOutcomeOpen -> "SPIRAL OPEN"
            let blockers =
                if List.isEmpty snapshot.blockers && terminalProtocolOpen then "terminal_protocol_open"
                elif List.isEmpty snapshot.blockers then "none"
                else snapshot.blockers |> List.map reducerHudBlockerText |> String.concat ","
            let discoveryText = match snapshot.discovery with | ReducerHudDiscoveryClosed -> "closed" | ReducerHudDiscoveryOpen reserve -> sprintf "open(reserve=%d)" reserve
            let crossKindText = match snapshot.crossKind with | ReducerHudCrossKindClear -> "clear" | ReducerHudCrossKindLive count -> sprintf "live(%d)" count
            let poisonText = match snapshot.cyclePoison with | ReducerHudCyclePoisonClear -> "clear" | ReducerHudCyclePoisonSuspected repeats -> sprintf "suspected(repeat=%d)" repeats | ReducerHudCyclePoisonQuarantined receipt -> sprintf "quarantined(receipt=%u)" receipt
            let hotNodeText = match snapshot.hotNode with | ReducerHudHotNodeUnknown -> "unknown" | ReducerHudHotNodeKnown(nodeId,path,line,kind,queue) -> FastRuntimeFormat.format "%s:%d node=%s kind=%s q=%d" [| box path; box line; box nodeId; box kind; box queue |]
            let criticalPathText =
                if terminalProtocolOpen then
                    sprintf "terminal_protocol(possession=%s|run_end_pending=%b)"
                        (reducerHudPossessionText snapshot.possession)
                        (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.runEndReceiptRef)
                else
                    reducerHudCriticalPathText snapshot.eta.criticalPath
            let cumulativeSemanticRate =
                if snapshot.elapsedMsAtSnapshot <= 0L || snapshot.work.semantic.retiredCost <= 0L then 0.0
                else float snapshot.work.semantic.retiredCost * 1000.0 / float snapshot.elapsedMsAtSnapshot
            let rateOrCumulative observed =
                if failedClosed && cumulativeSemanticRate > 0.0 then cumulativeSemanticRate
                elif System.Double.IsNaN observed || System.Double.IsInfinity observed || observed <= 0.0 then cumulativeSemanticRate
                else observed
            let shortRateDisplay = rateOrCumulative snapshot.rates.shortSemanticCostPerSecond
            let mediumRateDisplay = rateOrCumulative snapshot.rates.mediumSemanticCostPerSecond
            let sessionRateDisplay = rateOrCumulative snapshot.rates.sessionSemanticCostPerSecond
            let fusedRateDisplay = rateOrCumulative snapshot.rates.fusedSemanticCostPerSecond
            let rateDisplayAuthority =
                if failedClosed && cumulativeSemanticRate > 0.0 then "failed_closed_cumulative_retired_over_snapshot_elapsed"
                elif snapshot.rates.sessionSemanticCostPerSecond > 0.0 then snapshot.rates.rateAuthorityRef
                elif cumulativeSemanticRate > 0.0 then "cumulative_retired_over_snapshot_elapsed"
                else snapshot.rates.rateAuthorityRef
            [|
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "%s | terminal=%.6f%% | work=%.6f%% | elapsed=%s | eta=%s | total=%s" [| box outcomeLabel; box terminalProgressPct; box compileProgressPct; box elapsedText; box etaText; box totalText |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "semantic retired=%d total_mid=%d discovered=%d reserve_p50=%d reserve_p90=%d" [| box snapshot.work.semantic.retiredCost; box snapshot.work.semantic.totalMid; box snapshot.work.semantic.discoveredCost; box snapshot.work.semantic.reserveP50Cost; box snapshot.work.semantic.reserveP90Cost |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "ast completed=%d total=%d discovered=%d exact=%b source=%s" [| box snapshot.work.ast.completedCost; box snapshot.work.ast.totalCost; box snapshot.work.ast.discoveredCost; box snapshot.work.ast.exact; box snapshot.work.ast.sourceRef |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "remaining known=%d blocked=%d proven_dead=%d interval=[%.2f..%.2f]%% semantic_revision=%d" [| box snapshot.work.semantic.knownRemainingCost; box snapshot.work.semantic.blockedCost; box snapshot.work.semantic.provenDeadCost; box (float snapshot.work.lowBp / 100.0); box (float snapshot.work.highBp / 100.0); box snapshot.work.semantic.revision |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "rate phase=%s short=%.3f medium=%.3f session=%.3f fused=%.3f semantic_cost/s ref=%s" [| box (reducerHudProgressPhaseText snapshot.rates.phase); box shortRateDisplay; box mediumRateDisplay; box sessionRateDisplay; box fusedRateDisplay; box rateDisplayAuthority |]
                if failedClosed then
                    sprintf "eta=failed_closed confidence=unavailable samples=%d" snapshot.rates.samples
                elif terminalProtocolOpen then
                    sprintf "eta=terminal_protocol_open confidence=unavailable samples=%d" snapshot.rates.samples
                else
                    FastRuntimeFormat.format "eta phase=%s p50=%s p90=%s sigma=%s confidence=%.3f samples=%d ref=%s" [| box (reducerHudProgressPhaseText snapshot.eta.phase); box (etaMillisecondsText (reducerHudEtaP50Ms snapshot)); box (etaMillisecondsText (reducerHudEtaP90Ms snapshot)); box (etaMillisecondsText (reducerHudEtaSigmaMs snapshot)); box snapshot.rates.confidence; box snapshot.rates.samples; box snapshot.eta.rateAuthorityRef |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "timing cpu_exclusive=%s cpu_authority=%s wall_inclusive=%dms queue=%dms blocked_child=%dms receipt=%s" [| box (snapshot.timing.cpuExclusiveMs |> Option.map (fun value -> string value + "ms") |> Option.defaultValue "unavailable"); box (reducerHudCpuAuthorityText snapshot.timing.cpuAuthority); box snapshot.timing.wallInclusiveMs; box snapshot.timing.queueDelayMs; box snapshot.timing.blockedOnChildMs; box snapshot.timing.timingReceiptRef |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "phase=%s discovery=%s snapshot_age=%dms generation=%d" [| box (reducerHudProgressPhaseText snapshot.phase); box discoveryText; box ageMs; box snapshot.generation |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "possession=%s actor=%s stage_token=%s fill=%s run_end=%s physical_exit=%s exit_code=%s sealed_at_ms=%s" [| box (reducerHudPossessionText snapshot.possession); box snapshot.actorRef; box snapshot.stageTokenRef; box snapshot.fillReceiptRef; box snapshot.runEndReceiptRef; box snapshot.physicalExitReceiptRef; box (snapshot.exitCode |> Option.map string |> Option.defaultValue ""); box (snapshot.sealedAtMs |> Option.map string |> Option.defaultValue "") |]
                sprintf "blockers=[%s]" blockers
                sprintf "hot_node=%s" hotNodeText
                sprintf "critical_path=%s effective_parallelism=%.2f"
                    criticalPathText
                    snapshot.eta.effectiveParallelism
                sprintf "cross_kind=%s cycle_poison=%s" crossKindText poisonText
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "variance=%.4f exact_ast=%b exact_semantic=%b" [| box snapshot.rates.variance; box snapshot.work.ast.exact; box snapshot.work.semantic.exact |]
                sprintf "operational revision=%d semantic_epoch=%d" snapshot.operationalRevision snapshot.semanticEpoch
                sprintf "operational_graph_ref=%s" snapshot.operationalGraphRef
                sprintf "runtime_authority_ref=%s" snapshot.runtimeAuthorityRef
                sprintf "qap stage=%s generation_ref=%s" (reducerHudQapStageText snapshot.qapStage) snapshot.qapGenerationRef
                sprintf "terminal_snapshot_ref=%s" snapshot.terminalSnapshotRef
                sprintf "terminal_receipts commit=%s done=%s" snapshot.commitReceiptRef snapshot.doneReceiptRef
                sprintf "exit_receipts run_end=%s physical=%s" snapshot.runEndReceiptRef snapshot.physicalExitReceiptRef
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "work_exactness ast=%b semantic=%b discovery=%s" [| box snapshot.work.ast.exact; box snapshot.work.semantic.exact; box discoveryText |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "semantic totals low=%d mid=%d high=%d" [| box snapshot.work.semantic.totalLow; box snapshot.work.semantic.totalMid; box snapshot.work.semantic.totalHigh |]
                sprintf "semantic reserve p50=%d p90=%d" snapshot.work.semantic.reserveP50Cost snapshot.work.semantic.reserveP90Cost
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "rate_authority_ref=%s confidence=%.3f samples=%d" [| box rateDisplayAuthority; box snapshot.rates.confidence; box snapshot.rates.samples |]
                sprintf "eta_authority_ref=%s effective_parallelism=%.2f" snapshot.eta.rateAuthorityRef snapshot.eta.effectiveParallelism
                sprintf "timing_receipt_ref=%s" snapshot.timing.timingReceiptRef
                sprintf "blocker_count=%d hot_node_authority=reducer_snapshot" snapshot.blockers.Length
                sprintf "outcome=%s exit_code=%s" (reducerHudOutcomeText outcomeId) (snapshot.exitCode |> Option.map string |> Option.defaultValue "")
                sprintf "qap_generation_present=%b qap_stage=%s" (not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.qapGenerationRef)) (reducerHudQapStageText snapshot.qapStage)
                sprintf "terminal_protocol_open=%b failed_closed=%b" terminalProtocolOpen failedClosed
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "receipt_presence commit=%b done=%b run_end=%b physical=%b" [| box (not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.commitReceiptRef)); box (not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.doneReceiptRef)); box (not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.runEndReceiptRef)); box (not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace snapshot.physicalExitReceiptRef)) |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "progress_bp low=%d mid=%d high=%d" [| box snapshot.work.lowBp; box snapshot.work.midBp; box snapshot.work.highBp |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "semantic_gap known=%d blocked=%d proven_dead=%d" [| box snapshot.work.semantic.knownRemainingCost; box snapshot.work.semantic.blockedCost; box snapshot.work.semantic.provenDeadCost |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "rate_short_medium short=%.3f medium=%.3f cumulative=%.3f" [| box shortRateDisplay; box mediumRateDisplay; box cumulativeSemanticRate |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "rate_session_fused session=%.3f fused=%.3f authority=%s" [| box sessionRateDisplay; box fusedRateDisplay; box rateDisplayAuthority |]
                if failedClosed then "eta_ms unavailable reason=failed_closed"
                elif terminalProtocolOpen then "eta_ms unavailable reason=terminal_protocol_open"
                else FastRuntimeFormat.format "eta_ms p50=%d p90=%d sigma=%d" [| box (reducerHudEtaP50Ms snapshot); box (reducerHudEtaP90Ms snapshot); box (reducerHudEtaSigmaMs snapshot) |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "snapshot_clock snapshot_ms=%d elapsed_at_snapshot_ms=%d age_ms=%d" [| box snapshot.snapshotMs; box snapshot.elapsedMsAtSnapshot; box ageMs |]
                FastRuntimeFormat.format "terminal_coordinates actor=%s stage_token=%s fill=%s" [| box snapshot.actorRef; box snapshot.stageTokenRef; box snapshot.fillReceiptRef |]
                sprintf "terminal_receipt_pair run_end=%s physical_exit=%s" snapshot.runEndReceiptRef snapshot.physicalExitReceiptRef
                sprintf "authority_pair graph=%s runtime=%s" snapshot.operationalGraphRef snapshot.runtimeAuthorityRef
                sprintf "closure_flags semantic_closed_world_exact=%b discovery=%s exactness_basis=structural_seed_plus_returned_conserved_credit" snapshot.work.semantic.exact discoveryText
                sprintf "observer_contract json_reparse=false generation=%d" snapshot.generation
                sprintf "render_contract detail_rows=50 terminal_rows=0 placeholders=0"
                sprintf "taskbar_projection=reducer_snapshot_only semantic_epoch=%d" snapshot.semanticEpoch
                sprintf "qap_projection generation_ref=%s stage=%s" snapshot.qapGenerationRef (reducerHudQapStageText snapshot.qapStage)
                "detail_band=50_rows | terminal_band=0_rows | placeholder_rows=0"
                "authority=reducer_owned_snapshot | observer_json_reparse=false"
                "cadence=50ms | clock_diff=50ms | rows=50 | contract=detailed_flex_no_prune"
                sprintf "next=%s" (reducerHudNextActionText snapshot)
            |]

        let private hudRows = 50
        let private hudDetailedRowsRequired = 50
        do
            if hudRows <> hudDetailedRowsRequired then
                invalidOp "The Spiral live HUD contract requires exactly fifty detailed rows."
        let mutable private hudLines : string[] = [||]
        let mutable private hudRevision = 0L
        // Smooth frames read an immutable semantic-board projection instead of
        // contending on the durable HUD/file-log gate at 20 FPS.
        let private progressHudSemanticBoardGate = obj()
        let mutable private progressHudSemanticBoardSnapshot : string[] = [||]

        let private progressHudSemanticBoardRead () =
            lock progressHudSemanticBoardGate (fun () -> Array.copy progressHudSemanticBoardSnapshot)

        let private progressHudSemanticBoardWrite (lines:string array) =
            lock progressHudSemanticBoardGate (fun () ->
                progressHudSemanticBoardSnapshot <- Array.copy lines)
        type FinalHudPersistenceState =
            | FinalHudPending
            | FinalHudCommitted

        let mutable private finalHudPersistenceState = FinalHudPending
        let private finalHudCommitted () =
            match finalHudPersistenceState with
            | FinalHudCommitted -> true
            | FinalHudPending -> false

        let mutable private terminalShutdownRequested = false

        let progressHudPresentationClosedNow () =
            terminalShutdownRequested && finalHudCommitted()

        let mutable private splitInstalled = false
        let mutable private lastWindowWidth = 0
        let mutable private lastWindowHeight = 0
        let mutable private lastLogBottomRow = 0
        // Observer-only compatibility cache. Reducer, footer and physical exit never read it.
        let private observerHudTelemetryKey key =
            CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest.ofText "observer-hud-telemetry-field" key

        let private observerHudTelemetryCache =
            Dictionary<CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest, string>()

        type private ObserverHudTerminalEligibleLatchState =
            | ObserverHudTerminalEligibleOpen
            | ObserverHudTerminalEligibleLatched

        type private ObserverHudSemanticReceiptLatchState =
            | ObserverHudSemanticReceiptMissing
            | ObserverHudSemanticReceiptObserved

        let mutable private observerHudTerminalEligibleLatchState =
            ObserverHudTerminalEligibleOpen

        let mutable private observerHudSemanticReceiptLatchState =
            ObserverHudSemanticReceiptMissing

        let private hardSemanticImplSet = HashSet<CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest>()
        let mutable private hudRealtimeLastMs = 0L
        let mutable private hudRealtimeLastCpuMs = 0.0
        let mutable private hudElapsedPulseLastMs = 0L

        // MIGRATION: typed repaint seam for the HUD renderer.  The raw log remains
        // append-only, but interactive terminals need a prepaint before a long JSON
        // line can monopolize the console writer.
        type private HudPaintPhaseId =
            | HudPaintPreLogAppend
            | HudPaintPostLogAppend
            | HudPaintFinalSnapshot

        let private hudPaintPhaseText = function
            | HudPaintPreLogAppend -> "pre_log_append"
            | HudPaintPostLogAppend -> "post_log_append"
            | HudPaintFinalSnapshot -> "final_snapshot"

        let private hudStructuredAtoms (text:string) =
            if String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace text then []
            else
                text.ToLowerInvariant().Split(
                    [| '_'; '-'; '|'; ':'; '/'; ' '; '\t'; '\r'; '\n'; '('; ')'; '['; ']'; '{'; '}'; ','; ';'; '='; '"'; '\'' |],
                    StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)
                |> Array.toList

        let rec private hudAtomsContainPair left right = function
            | x :: y :: _ when x = left && y = right -> true
            | _ :: tail -> hudAtomsContainPair left right tail
            | [] -> false

        type private HudGapSignalId =
            | HudGapCoalesced
            | HudGapLagging
            | HudGapOther

        let private hudGapSignalId text =
            let atoms = hudStructuredAtoms text |> Set.ofList
            if Set.contains "coalesced" atoms then HudGapCoalesced
            elif Set.contains "lag" atoms || Set.contains "lagging" atoms then HudGapLagging
            else HudGapOther

        type private HudDataFreshnessId =
            | HudDataFresh
            | HudDataLagging
            | HudDataCoalesced
            | HudDataStale
            | HudDataUnknown

        let private hudDataFreshnessText = function
            | HudDataFresh -> "fresh"
            | HudDataLagging -> "lagging"
            | HudDataCoalesced -> "coalesced"
            | HudDataStale -> "stale"
            | HudDataUnknown -> "unknown"

        let private hudDataFreshnessFor (richAgeText: string) (gapText: string) (staleText: string) =
            let mutable richAge = -1L
            let parsedAge = Int64.TryParse((if isNull richAgeText then "" else richAgeText).Trim(), &richAge)
            let gap = if isNull gapText then "" else gapText
            let stale = if isNull staleText then "" else staleText
            let gapSignal = hudGapSignalId gap
            if stale.Equals("true", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) then HudDataStale
            elif gapSignal = HudGapCoalesced then HudDataCoalesced
            elif gapSignal = HudGapLagging then HudDataLagging
            elif parsedAge && richAge >= 5000L then HudDataStale
            elif parsedAge && richAge >= 1500L then HudDataLagging
            elif parsedAge || not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace gap) then HudDataFresh
            else HudDataUnknown

        // MIGRATION: HUD layout and file graph are policy, not string drift.
        // Operator contract: the live compilation board is a fixed fifty-row TUI.
        // It is not a telemetry optimization surface and must not be pruned by
        // future assessment-driven compaction. Width adapts; information density stays.
        type private HudLayoutId =
            | HudLayoutTall50FileGraph

        let private hudLayoutId = HudLayoutTall50FileGraph

        let private hudLayoutText = function
            | HudLayoutTall50FileGraph -> "tall_50_smart_file_graph_no_prune"

        type private HudFileGraphModeId =
            | HudFileGraphDisabled
            | HudFileGraphTopFiles
            | HudFileGraphTreeGrid

        let private hudFileGraphModeText = function
            | HudFileGraphDisabled -> "disabled"
            | HudFileGraphTopFiles -> "top_files"
            | HudFileGraphTreeGrid -> "tree_grid"

        type private HudAuthorityDisplayId =
            | HudAuthorityCold
            | HudAuthorityReplayNoRoot
            | HudAuthoritySparseRootNoSemantic
            | HudAuthorityRootOrDriver
            | HudAuthorityTerminalOrSemantic

        let private hudAuthorityDisplayText = function
            | HudAuthorityCold -> "cold"
            | HudAuthorityReplayNoRoot -> "replay_no_root"
            | HudAuthoritySparseRootNoSemantic -> "sparse_root_no_semantic"
            | HudAuthorityRootOrDriver -> "root_or_driver"
            | HudAuthorityTerminalOrSemantic -> "terminal_or_semantic"

        // MIGRATION: replay-root finalization is now a HUD/state DU instead
        // of being inferred from loosely related replay_done/write_wit/root counters.
        type private ReplayRootFinalizationStateId =
            | ReplayRootFinalizationCold
            | ReplayRootFinalizationRequested
            | ReplayRootFinalizationDraining
            | ReplayRootFinalizationHandoffReady
            | ReplayRootFinalizationExhausted

        let private replayRootFinalizationStateText = function
            | ReplayRootFinalizationCold -> "cold"
            | ReplayRootFinalizationRequested -> "requested"
            | ReplayRootFinalizationDraining -> "draining"
            | ReplayRootFinalizationHandoffReady -> "handoff_ready"
            | ReplayRootFinalizationExhausted -> "exhausted"

        // MIGRATION: these were drifting as raw strings inside the HUD.
        // Keep row frequency independent from append-log frequency and make
        // graph density visible without turning it into a progress claim.
        type private HudRefreshModeId =
            | HudRefreshMinimal250ms
            | HudRefreshRichSnapshot

        let private hudRefreshModeText = function
            | HudRefreshMinimal250ms -> "minimal_250ms"
            | HudRefreshRichSnapshot -> "rich_snapshot"

        type private HudGraphDensityId =
            | HudGraphEmpty
            | HudGraphSparse
            | HudGraphDense
            | HudGraphHot

        let private hudGraphDensityFor fileCount totalEvents =
            if fileCount <= 0 || totalEvents <= 0L then HudGraphEmpty
            elif totalEvents < 16L then HudGraphSparse
            elif totalEvents < 128L then HudGraphDense
            else HudGraphHot

        let private hudGraphDensityText = function
            | HudGraphEmpty -> "empty"
            | HudGraphSparse -> "sparse"
            | HudGraphDense -> "dense"
            | HudGraphHot -> "hot"

        let private hudFileHeat = Dictionary<CompilerIdentityKernel.WorkSiteId, int64>()
        let private hudFileHeatLast = Dictionary<CompilerIdentityKernel.WorkSiteId, int64>()
        let private hudFileKinds = Dictionary<CompilerIdentityKernel.WorkSiteId, string>()
        let mutable private hudFileHeatTotal = 0L

        let private esc = "\u001b["

        let private supportsHud () =
            try
                // MIGRATION: hardcoded policy.  Interactive stderr gets ANSI bottom HUD;
                // redirected stderr gets plain JSONL.  No environment variables or host
                // switches participate in the compiler contract.
                (not Console.IsErrorRedirected)
                && Console.WindowHeight >= hudRows + 8
                && Console.WindowWidth >= 80
            with _ -> false

        let private appendHudEnabled () = false

        // MIGRATION: persistent per-run file mirror for the console stream.
        // The normal stderr JSONL/HUD contract remains unchanged; this sink is
        // additive and uses the same HUD gate so multi-core writes cannot jumble.
        type private CompilerFileLogStateId =
            | CompilerFileLogOpen of FileStream
            | CompilerFileLogDisabled of CompilerIdentityKernel.OperationalReasonId

        let private fileLogSourceDirectory = __SOURCE_DIRECTORY__
        let private fileLogStartedStamp = DateTime.Now.ToString("yyyyMMddHHmmss", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)
        let private fileLogPath = Path.Combine(fileLogSourceDirectory, fileLogStartedStamp + ".jsonl")
        let mutable private fileLogState : CompilerFileLogStateId option = None
        let mutable private fileLogPendingLineCount = 0
        let mutable private fileLogLastFlushMs = 0L
        let private fileLogFlushLineBudget = 32
        let private fileLogFlushCadenceMs = 100L
        let private fileLogUtf8 = new UTF8Encoding(false)

        let private fileLogEscJson (s: string) =
            let s = if isNull s then "" else s
            "\"" + s.Replace("\\","\\\\").Replace("\"","\\\"").Replace("\r","\\r").Replace("\n","\\n").Replace("\t","\\t") + "\""

        let private initFileLogUnlocked () =
            match fileLogState with
            | Some state -> state
            | None when System.String.Equals(System.Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable "SPIRAL_DIAG_QUIET", "1", System.StringComparison.Ordinal) ->
                // Quiet (batch) runs keep no per-process JSONL mirror: nobody reads it, its writes and flushes
                // were ~4% of a compile, and a day of suite runs once filled the disk with them.
                let state = CompilerFileLogDisabled (CompilerIdentityKernel.OperationalReasonIdOps.create "SPIRAL_DIAG_QUIET")
                fileLogState <- Some state
                state
            | None ->
                try
                    Directory.CreateDirectory(fileLogSourceDirectory) |> ignore
                    // The JSONL contract has one in-process writer authority.  Permit readers,
                    // but reject a second writer handle so accidental bypass paths cannot create
                    // torn/sparse records under concurrent emission.
                    let fs = new FileStream(fileLogPath, FileMode.OpenOrCreate, FileAccess.Write, FileShare.Read, 4096)
                    fs.Seek(0L, SeekOrigin.End) |> ignore
                    let state = CompilerFileLogOpen fs
                    fileLogState <- Some state
                    let startedLine =
                        FastRuntimeFormat.format "{\"v\":1,\"kind\":\"compiler_file_log_started\",\"source\":\"CompilerConsoleHud88\",\"policy\":\"single_host_process_jsonl|locked_direct_utf8_append_seek_end|flush_100ms_or_32_lines_terminal_immediate|final_hud_owned_by_writer\",\"source_directory\":%s,\"path\":%s,\"started_stamp\":%s}" [| box (fileLogEscJson fileLogSourceDirectory); box (fileLogEscJson fileLogPath); box (fileLogEscJson fileLogStartedStamp) |]
                    let startedBytes = fileLogUtf8.GetBytes(startedLine + "\n")
                    fs.Write(startedBytes, 0, startedBytes.Length)
                    fs.Flush()
                    fileLogPendingLineCount <- 0
                    fileLogLastFlushMs <- DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds()
                    state
                with ex ->
                    let state = CompilerFileLogDisabled (CompilerIdentityKernel.OperationalReasonIdOps.create ex.Message)
                    fileLogState <- Some state
                    state

        let private fileLogWriteGate = obj()

        type private CompilerFileLogLineKindId =
            | CompilerFileLogTerminalPresentationEpilogue
            | CompilerFileLogReducerHudFinalSnapshot
            | CompilerFileLogSpiralHudFinal
            | CompilerFileLogRunEnd
            | CompilerFileLogTerminalFamily
            | CompilerFileLogBuildErrorTraceFamily
            | CompilerFileLogOther

        let private compilerFileLogLineKindFor (line:string) =
            if Object.ReferenceEquals(line, null) then
                CompilerFileLogOther
            else
                let parts = line.Split([|"\"kind\":\""|], 2, StringSplitOptions.None)
                let kind =
                    if parts.Length <> 2 then ""
                    else
                        parts.[1].Split([|'"'|], 2)
                        |> Array.tryHead
                        |> Option.defaultValue ""
                let atoms =
                    if String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace kind then []
                    else kind.Split([|'_'|], StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries) |> Array.toList
                match kind, atoms with
                | "terminal_presentation_epilogue", _ -> CompilerFileLogTerminalPresentationEpilogue
                | "reducer_hud_final_snapshot", _ -> CompilerFileLogReducerHudFinalSnapshot
                | "spiral_hud_final", _ -> CompilerFileLogSpiralHudFinal
                | "run_end", _ -> CompilerFileLogRunEnd
                | _, "terminal" :: _ -> CompilerFileLogTerminalFamily
                | _, "build" :: "error" :: "trace" :: _ -> CompilerFileLogBuildErrorTraceFamily
                | _ -> CompilerFileLogOther

        let private compilerFileLogFramedLine (s:string) =
            if Object.ReferenceEquals(s, null) then s
            else
                let mutable containsNul = false
                let mutable containsRawControl = false
                let mutable i = 0
                while not containsRawControl && i < s.Length do
                    let c = s.[i]
                    if c = '\u0000' then containsNul <- true
                    if int c < 32 then containsRawControl <- true
                    i <- i + 1
                let startsObject = s.Length > 0 && s.[0] = '{'
                let endsObject = s.Length > 1 && s.[s.Length - 1] = '}'
                if startsObject && endsObject && not containsRawControl then s
                else
                    let lineRef =
                        CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest.ofText "compiler-file-log-malformed-line" s
                        |> CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest.text
                    FastRuntimeFormat.format
                        "{\"v\":1,\"kind\":\"compiler_file_log_malformed_line_rejected\",\"line_ref\":%s,\"original_length\":%d,\"starts_object\":%b,\"ends_object\":%b,\"contains_nul\":%b,\"contains_raw_control\":%b,\"authority\":\"single_writer_frame_validation_before_stream_write\",\"next\":\"correlate_producer_by_adjacent_typed_receipts\"}"
                        [| box (fileLogEscJson lineRef); box s.Length; box startsObject; box endsObject; box containsNul; box containsRawControl |]

        let private appendFileLogLineSerialized (s: string) =
            let s = compilerFileLogFramedLine s
            let lineKind = compilerFileLogLineKindFor s
            let footerOwnedLine =
                match lineKind with
                | CompilerFileLogTerminalPresentationEpilogue
                | CompilerFileLogReducerHudFinalSnapshot
                | CompilerFileLogSpiralHudFinal -> true
                | _ -> false
            let immediateFlush =
                match lineKind with
                | CompilerFileLogTerminalPresentationEpilogue
                | CompilerFileLogReducerHudFinalSnapshot
                | CompilerFileLogSpiralHudFinal
                | CompilerFileLogRunEnd
                | CompilerFileLogTerminalFamily
                | CompilerFileLogBuildErrorTraceFamily -> true
                | CompilerFileLogOther -> false
            if not (Object.ReferenceEquals(s, null))
               && (not terminalShutdownRequested || footerOwnedLine)
               && not (terminalShutdownRequested && finalHudCommitted()) then
                lock fileLogWriteGate (fun () ->
                    match initFileLogUnlocked() with
                    | CompilerFileLogOpen fs ->
                        try
                            // A JSONL frame has one physical append authority.  Seek to the
                            // current end for every complete frame so a stale file position can
                            // never create a sparse NUL hole after truncation or host interference.
                            fs.Seek(0L, SeekOrigin.End) |> ignore
                            let frameBytes = fileLogUtf8.GetBytes(s + "\n")
                            fs.Write(frameBytes, 0, frameBytes.Length)
                            fileLogPendingLineCount <- fileLogPendingLineCount + 1
                            let nowMs = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds()
                            let flushDue =
                                immediateFlush
                                || fileLogPendingLineCount >= fileLogFlushLineBudget
                                || fileLogLastFlushMs = 0L
                                || nowMs - fileLogLastFlushMs >= fileLogFlushCadenceMs
                            if flushDue then
                                fs.Flush()
                                fileLogPendingLineCount <- 0
                                fileLogLastFlushMs <- nowMs
                        with ex ->
                            fileLogState <- Some (CompilerFileLogDisabled (CompilerIdentityKernel.OperationalReasonIdOps.create ex.Message))
                    | CompilerFileLogDisabled _ ->
                        ())

        // MIGRATION: catch exception evidence before console-only handlers erase it.
        // First-chance capture is sparse and deduplicated; unhandled/unobserved paths
        // persist only bounded typed message data plus the CLR stack.
        type private ExceptionCaptureReentryState =
            | ExceptionCaptureIdle
            | ExceptionCaptureActive

        let private exceptionCaptureGate = obj()
        let private exceptionCaptureReentryGate = obj()
        let private exceptionCaptureCounts = Dictionary<CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest, int64>()
        let mutable private exceptionCaptureHooksInstalled = false
        let mutable private exceptionCaptureReentryState = ExceptionCaptureIdle
        let mutable private exceptionCaptureUnique = 0

        let private tryEnterExceptionCapture () =
            lock exceptionCaptureReentryGate (fun () ->
                match exceptionCaptureReentryState with
                | ExceptionCaptureIdle ->
                    exceptionCaptureReentryState <- ExceptionCaptureActive
                    true
                | ExceptionCaptureActive -> false)

        let private leaveExceptionCapture () =
            lock exceptionCaptureReentryGate (fun () ->
                exceptionCaptureReentryState <- ExceptionCaptureIdle)

        let private exceptionCaptureMilestone count =
            count <= 3L
            || (count > 0L && (count &&& (count - 1L)) = 0L)
            || count % 64L = 0L

        type RuntimeExceptionCapturePayloadBasis =
            | RuntimeExceptionBoundedTypedMessagePlusClrStack

        let private runtimeExceptionTypeName (ex:exn) =
            if isNull ex then "null"
            else
                let typeName = ex.GetType().FullName
                if isNull typeName then ex.GetType().Name else typeName

        let private runtimeExceptionStackTrace (ex:exn) =
            if isNull ex then ""
            else
                try
                    let stack = ex.StackTrace
                    if isNull stack then "" else stack
                with _ -> ""

        let private runtimeExceptionBoundedSemanticMessage (ex:exn) =
            if isNull ex then None
            else
                try
                    let exceptionType = ex.GetType()
                    let compactBounded (message:string) =
                        let compact = message.Replace("\r", " ").Replace("\n", " ").Replace("\t", " ")
                        if compact.Length <= 512 then compact else compact.Substring(0, 512)
                    let fieldText name =
                        let property = exceptionType.GetProperty(name)
                        if isNull property then ""
                        else
                            match property.GetValue(ex) with
                            | null -> ""
                            | value -> string value
                    match exceptionType.Name with
                    | "PartEvalTypeError" ->
                        let message = fieldText "Data1"
                        if message = "" then None else Some(compactBounded message)
                    | "EvalVisitBudgetFailure" ->
                        Some(
                            FastRuntimeFormat.format "EvalVisitBudgetFailure(kind=%s|key=%s|site=%s|visit=%s/%s|unproductive_streak=%s|unproductive_age_ms=%s)" [| box (fieldText "Data0"); box (fieldText "Data1"); box (fieldText "Data2"); box (fieldText "Data3"); box (fieldText "Data4"); box (fieldText "Data5"); box (fieldText "Data6") |]
                            |> compactBounded)
                    | "InvalidOperationException" ->
                        // System.InvalidOperationException owns a materialized string message;
                        // unlike recursive F# union/list payload formatters it is safe to bound here.
                        let message = ex.Message
                        if isNull message || message = "" then None else Some(compactBounded message)
                    | _ -> None
                with _ -> None

        let private runtimeExceptionStructuredFieldsJson (ex:exn) =
            if isNull ex then ""
            else
                try
                    let exceptionType = ex.GetType()
                    let tryField name =
                        let property = exceptionType.GetProperty(name)
                        if isNull property then None
                        else
                            try Some (property.GetValue(ex))
                            with _ -> None
                    let fieldText name =
                        match tryField name with
                        | Some null
                        | None -> ""
                        | Some value ->
                            let text = string value
                            if text.Length <= 512 then text else text.Substring(0, 512)
                    let fieldInt name =
                        match tryField name with
                        | Some (:? int as value) -> value
                        | _ -> 0
                    let fieldInt64 name =
                        match tryField name with
                        | Some (:? int64 as value) -> value
                        | Some (:? int as value) -> int64 value
                        | _ -> 0L
                    match exceptionType.Name with
                    | "EvalVisitBudgetFailure" ->
                        FastRuntimeFormat.format ",\"eval_visit_kind_du\":%s,\"eval_visit_key\":%s,\"eval_visit_site\":%s,\"eval_visit_count\":%d,\"eval_visit_budget\":%d,\"eval_visit_unproductive_streak\":%d,\"eval_visit_unproductive_age_ms\":%d,\"typed_projection_available\":true" [| box (fileLogEscJson (fieldText "Data0")); box (fileLogEscJson (fieldText "Data1")); box (fileLogEscJson (fieldText "Data2")); box (fieldInt "Data3"); box (fieldInt "Data4"); box (fieldInt "Data5"); box (fieldInt64 "Data6") |]
                    | _ -> ",\"typed_projection_available\":false"
                with _ -> ",\"typed_projection_available\":false"

        let private exceptionCaptureKey (ex:exn) =
            let typeName = runtimeExceptionTypeName ex
            let stack = runtimeExceptionStackTrace ex
            let identityText = typeName + "|" + (if stack.Length <= 512 then stack else stack.Substring(0, 512))
            CompilerIdentityKernel.ContentDigest.ofText "runtime-exception-capture" identityText

        let private captureRuntimeException kind source (ex:exn) =
            if not (isNull ex)
               && not (ex :? OperationCanceledException)
               && not (ex :? System.Threading.Tasks.TaskCanceledException) then
                let key = exceptionCaptureKey ex
                let count, accepted =
                    lock exceptionCaptureGate (fun () ->
                        let mutable prior = 0L
                        let known = exceptionCaptureCounts.TryGetValue(key, &prior)
                        if known then
                            let next = prior + 1L
                            exceptionCaptureCounts.[key] <- next
                            next, exceptionCaptureMilestone next
                        elif exceptionCaptureUnique < 256 then
                            exceptionCaptureUnique <- exceptionCaptureUnique + 1
                            exceptionCaptureCounts.[key] <- 1L
                            1L, true
                        else
                            1L, false)
                if accepted && tryEnterExceptionCapture () then
                    try
                        // Never call ex.Message or ex.ToString here. F# exception fields may
                        // contain very deep semantic lists, and their generated formatter is
                        // recursive. For PartEvalTypeError only, reflect the already-materialized
                        // string payload and cap it before emitting the CLR stack.
                        let semanticMessage = runtimeExceptionBoundedSemanticMessage ex
                        let structuredFields = runtimeExceptionStructuredFieldsJson ex
                        let payloadRaw = runtimeExceptionStackTrace ex
                        let payloadCap = 8192
                        let payloadTruncated = payloadRaw.Length > payloadCap
                        let payload = if payloadTruncated then payloadRaw.Substring(0, payloadCap) else payloadRaw
                        let line =
                            FastRuntimeFormat.format "{\"v\":1,\"kind\":\"runtime_exception_captured\",\"capture_kind_du\":%s,\"source\":%s,\"exception_type\":%s,\"semantic_message\":%s,\"semantic_message_available\":%s%s,\"payload_basis_du\":\"RuntimeExceptionBoundedTypedProjectionPlusClrStack\",\"stack_trace\":%s,\"stack_trace_chars\":%d,\"stack_trace_truncated\":%s,\"occurrence\":%d,\"thread_id\":%d,\"policy\":\"runtime_boundary_reflects_only_bounded_typed_fields_never_recursive_exception_formatter\"}" [| box (fileLogEscJson kind); box (fileLogEscJson source); box (fileLogEscJson (runtimeExceptionTypeName ex)); box (semanticMessage |> Option.defaultValue "" |> fileLogEscJson); box (if semanticMessage.IsSome then "true" else "false"); box structuredFields; box (fileLogEscJson payload); box payloadRaw.Length; box (if payloadTruncated then "true" else "false"); box count; box Thread.CurrentThread.ManagedThreadId |]
                        let mutable taken = false
                        try
                            Monitor.TryEnter(gate, 25, &taken) |> ignore
                            if taken then appendFileLogLineSerialized line
                        finally
                            if taken then Monitor.Exit(gate)
                    finally
                        leaveExceptionCapture ()

        let captureWorkerBoundaryException source (ex:exn) =
            captureRuntimeException "worker_boundary" source ex

        let captureBuildBoundaryException source (ex:exn) =
            captureRuntimeException "build_boundary" source ex

        // Public reducer failure helpers intentionally live beside the durable HUD/file writer.
        // External callers must qualify CompilerConsoleHud88 rather than DiagJson so declaration ownership stays explicit.
        let captureReducerBoundaryException source (ex:exn) =
            captureRuntimeException "reducer_boundary" source ex

        let emitImmediateFailureEvent kind source correlation message next =
            let compactBounded (value:string) =
                let value = if isNull value then "" else value.Replace("\r", " ").Replace("\n", " ").Replace("\t", " ")
                if value.Length <= 768 then value else value.Substring(0, 768)
            let line =
                FastRuntimeFormat.format
                    "{\"v\":1,\"ts_ms\":%d,\"pid\":%d,\"tid\":%d,\"kind\":%s,\"source\":%s,\"correlation\":%s,\"message\":%s,\"authority\":\"immediate_failure_boundary_before_control_transfer\",\"next\":%s,\"payload_policy_du\":\"BoundedStructuredContextNoRecursiveExceptionFormatting\"}"
                    [| box (DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds()); box (System.Environment.ProcessId); box Thread.CurrentThread.ManagedThreadId; box (fileLogEscJson (compactBounded kind)); box (fileLogEscJson (compactBounded source)); box (fileLogEscJson (compactBounded correlation)); box (fileLogEscJson (compactBounded message)); box (fileLogEscJson (compactBounded next)) |]
            appendFileLogLineSerialized line

        let private installRuntimeExceptionCaptureHooks () =
            let shouldInstall =
                lock exceptionCaptureGate (fun () ->
                    if exceptionCaptureHooksInstalled then false
                    else
                        exceptionCaptureHooksInstalled <- true
                        true)
            if shouldInstall then
                // MIGRATION: FirstChanceException is intentionally not subscribed.
                // Spiral uses PartEvalTypeError as control flow; global first-chance
                // capture serialized enormous expected stacks and stole CPU/HUD time.
                try AppDomain.CurrentDomain.UnhandledException.Add(fun args ->
                    match args.ExceptionObject with
                    | :? exn as ex -> captureRuntimeException "unhandled" "AppDomain.UnhandledException" ex
                    | _ -> ()) with _ -> ()
                try System.Threading.Tasks.TaskScheduler.UnobservedTaskException.Add(fun args ->
                    captureRuntimeException "unobserved_task" "TaskScheduler.UnobservedTaskException" args.Exception) with _ -> ()

        let private safeWidth () =
            try max 60 (Console.WindowWidth - 1)
            with _ -> 120

        let private safeHeight () =
            try max (hudRows + 6) Console.WindowHeight
            with _ -> hudRows + 6

        let private logBottomRow0 () =
            max 0 ((safeHeight()) - hudRows - 1)

        let private hudStartRow0 () =
            max 0 ((safeHeight()) - hudRows)

        type private ProgressHudConsoleLane =
            | ProgressHudConsoleStderrUnified
            | ProgressHudConsoleRedirectedFallback

        let private progressHudConsoleLaneText = function
            | ProgressHudConsoleStderrUnified -> "stderr_unified_atomic_compositor"
            | ProgressHudConsoleRedirectedFallback -> "stderr_redirected_append_only"

        type private ProgressHudFlushPolicy =
            | ProgressHudFlushBuffered
            | ProgressHudFlushRedirectedEachFrame

        let private progressHudFlushPolicyFor = function
            | ProgressHudConsoleStderrUnified -> ProgressHudFlushBuffered
            | ProgressHudConsoleRedirectedFallback -> ProgressHudFlushRedirectedEachFrame

        let private progressHudFlushPolicyText = function
            | ProgressHudFlushBuffered -> "buffered_terminal_stream"
            | ProgressHudFlushRedirectedEachFrame -> "redirected_flush_each_visible_frame"

        // MIGRATION: ANSI scroll-region control, JSON console lines and HUD frames
        // must share one stream and one arbiter. The MIGRATION stdout HUD could
        // race stderr JSON, so the terminal cursor state was never atomic.
        let private progressHudConsoleWriteGate = obj()
        let private progressHudDiffGate = obj()
        let mutable private progressHudLastRenderedLines : string array = [||]
        let mutable private progressHudLastRenderedWidth = -1
        let mutable private progressHudLastRenderedStart = -1

        let private invalidateProgressHudDiffCache () =
            lock progressHudDiffGate (fun () ->
                progressHudLastRenderedLines <- [||]
                progressHudLastRenderedWidth <- -1
                progressHudLastRenderedStart <- -1)

        let private progressHudWriterAndLane () =
            try
                if not Console.IsErrorRedirected then Console.Error, ProgressHudConsoleStderrUnified
                else Console.Error, ProgressHudConsoleRedirectedFallback
            with _ -> Console.Error, ProgressHudConsoleRedirectedFallback

        let progressHudVisibleConsoleLaneText () =
            let _, lane = progressHudWriterAndLane()
            progressHudConsoleLaneText lane

        let progressHudVisibleFlushPolicyText () =
            let _, lane = progressHudWriterAndLane()
            lane |> progressHudFlushPolicyFor |> progressHudFlushPolicyText

        let private ansi (s: string) =
            lock progressHudConsoleWriteGate (fun () -> Console.Error.Write(s))

        let private cleanText (s: string) =
            if String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace s then ""
            else s.Replace("\r", " ").Replace("\n", " ").Replace("\t", " ")

        // MIGRATION: HUD formatting must never be the final fatal silence.
        // Emit exception type/message/stack as JSONL, then replay the raw line.
        let private emitHudExceptionUnlocked (scope: string) (line: string) (ex: exn) =
            try
                let escJson (s: string) =
                    let s = if isNull s then "" else s
                    "\"" + s.Replace("\\","\\\\").Replace("\"","\\\"").Replace("\r","\\r").Replace("\n","\\n").Replace("\t","\\t") + "\""
                let stack = if isNull ex.StackTrace then "" else ex.StackTrace
                let payload =
                    FastRuntimeFormat.format "{\"kind\":\"spiral_hud_format_exception\",\"scope\":%s,\"exception_type\":%s,\"message\":%s,\"stack\":%s,\"policy\":\"safe_hud_try_with_emits_stacktrace_no_silent_dotnet_crash\",\"next\":\"continue_compiler_after_hud_failure\"}" [| box (escJson scope); box (escJson (ex.GetType().FullName)); box (escJson ex.Message); box (escJson stack) |]
                let mutable taken = false
                try
                    Monitor.TryEnter(gate, 25, &taken) |> ignore
                    if taken then
                        appendFileLogLineSerialized payload
                        if not (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace line) then appendFileLogLineSerialized line
                finally
                    if taken then Monitor.Exit(gate)
            with _ -> ()

        let private trimTo width (s: string) =
            let s = cleanText s
            if width <= 0 then ""
            elif s.Length <= width then s
            elif width = 1 then s.Substring(0, 1)
            else s.Substring(0, width)

        let private fitLine width (s: string) =
            (trimTo width s).PadRight(width)

        let private colR width (s: string) =
            let s =
                let x = cleanText s
                if String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace x then "-"
                else x
            let s = if s.Length > width then s.Substring(0, width) else s
            // MIGRATION: keep columns stable with trailing blanks after each value,
            // matching the requested "spacing to the right of values" HUD layout.
            s.PadRight(width)

        let private colL width (s: string) =
            let s =
                let x = cleanText s
                if String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace x then "-"
                else x
            let s = if s.Length > width then s.Substring(0, width) else s
            s.PadRight(width)

        let private fmtFloat width digits (s: string) =
            let mutable v = 0.0
            if Double.TryParse(s, NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, &v) then
                colR width (v.ToString("F" + string digits, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))
            else colR width s

        let private pairR name width value =
            sprintf "%s=%s" name (colR width value)

        let private pairL name width value =
            sprintf "%s=%s" name (colL width value)

        let private pairF name width digits value =
            sprintf "%s=%s" name (fmtFloat width digits value)

        let private hudRule (title: string) =
            let label = " " + cleanText title + " "
            let fill = max 0 (116 - label.Length)
            "+" + label + String('-', fill) + "+"

        let private hudFlex4 (a: string) (b: string) (c: string) (d: string) =
            FastRuntimeFormat.format "| %s | %s | %s | %s |" [| box (fitLine 26 a); box (fitLine 26 b); box (fitLine 26 c); box (fitLine 26 d) |]

        let private hudFlex3 (a: string) (b: string) (c: string) =
            FastRuntimeFormat.format "| %s | %s | %s |" [| box (fitLine 36 a); box (fitLine 36 b); box (fitLine 36 c) |]

        let private hudFlex2 (a: string) (b: string) =
            sprintf "| %s | %s |" (fitLine 56 a) (fitLine 57 b)

        let private hudKv (k: string) (v: string) =
            sprintf "%s=%s" (trimTo 13 k) (cleanText v)

        let private hudKvWide (k: string) (v: string) =
            sprintf "%s=%s" (trimTo 16 k) (cleanText v)

        type HudKindOtherKind private () =
            static member InternedKindTag () = 0x120003u
        type HudKindOtherId = CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId<HudKindOtherKind>

        module HudKindOtherIdOps =
            let create value : HudKindOtherId = CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextId.create<HudKindOtherKind> value
            let text (value:HudKindOtherId) = CompilerIdentityKernel.InternedTextIdOps.text value

        type HudKindId =
            | HudKindEmpty
            | HudKindTerminal
            | HudKindCycle
            | HudKindParentReplay
            | HudKindReplayDriver
            | HudKindReplay
            | HudKindProgressTick
            | HudKindWork
            | HudKindSpiralHud
            | HudKindSemantic
            | HudKindSourceValue
            | HudKindOther of HudKindOtherId

        let private hudKindId (kind:string) =
            let k = cleanText kind
            let atoms = hudStructuredAtoms k
            match atoms with
            | [] -> HudKindEmpty
            | "eval" :: "worklist" :: "terminal" :: _ -> HudKindTerminal
            | _ when hudAtomsContainPair "cycle" "break" atoms -> HudKindCycle
            | _ when hudAtomsContainPair "parent" "replay" atoms -> HudKindParentReplay
            | _ when hudAtomsContainPair "replay" "driver" atoms -> HudKindReplayDriver
            | _ when hudAtomsContainPair "progress" "tick" atoms -> HudKindProgressTick
